{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon","id":609481,"title":"Vampire the Masquerade 4th Edition announced at Gencon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-31T08:35:15-07:00","id":609481,"title":"Vampire the Masquerade 4th Edition announced at Gencon?","content":"Wow, is this real?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://plus.google.com/+BrycePerry/posts/ga2xnRi7a7p\" target=\"_blank\">https://plus.google.com/+BrycePerry/posts/ga2xnRi7a7p<br /> <br /> &quot;</a><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">BREAKING NEWS! VAMPIRE THE MASQUERADE 4TH EDITION ANNOUNCED AT GENCON! Due next year for 25th anniversary! Updated system, advanced metaplot&quot;</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5402-malcolmlittle","user":"MalcolmLittle","date":". 07-31-2015, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5402-malcolmlittle","name":"MalcolmLittle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:37:34-07:00","id":609509,"title":"","content":"Link to the announcement on OPP's twitter feed.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/TheOnyxPath/status/627133072199274496\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/TheOnyxPath/stat...33072199274496</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:40:22-07:00","id":609513,"title":"","content":"About time!<br /> <br /> I love <b>V20</b> dearly, but compared to the following 'Twentieth Anniversary' versions (<b>W20</b> and especially <b>M20</b>), it feels like <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b> got a polished-up omnibus rather than a proper new edition. I'm soooo happy, but my bank account is soooo sad.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Unless this turns out to be some kind of sad prank... And that would be just the worst! As it stands, though, I hope it would be a retooling of <b>V20</b> as a proper Fourth Edition, similar to how <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b>'s Second Edition <i>was</i> called <i>Blood and Smoke</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":409,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","user":"Phaolan","date":". 07-31-2015, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:43:25-07:00","id":609516,"title":"","content":"I'm feeling kinda... meh? On doing a 4th edition of the cWOD; for all I think it needs one. Let the cWOD devs and authors finish the 20th lines at least? Or at least make them highly compatible...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:49:34-07:00","id":609522,"title":"","content":"YES! my wish came true!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:55:54-07:00","id":609528,"title":"","content":"Awesome news! Very happy to hear this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T08:58:38-07:00","id":609530,"title":"","content":"I kinda thought V20 <i>was</i> the 4th edition. I'm not sure how I feel about this news, tbh. I kinda wish they waited until they revised the rest of the lines before putting out yet another VtM update, but I'll still be buying it. Cuz I'm <i>that</i> kind of sucker who wants to own <i>everything</i> from the cWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:30:11-07:00","id":609601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609516#post609516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let the cWOD devs and authors finish the 20th lines at least? Or at least make them highly compatible...</div> </div> </div> </div>They do clarify later that it's not coming until the current V20 run is completely finished.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Before enlightenment: chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment: Glorious Tree-Felling Prana and All-Encompassing Liquid-Carrying Methodology.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1223-dorchadas","name":"Dorchadas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1223_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:44:41-07:00","id":609613,"title":"","content":"Would like it if they published a proper game that was old universe and metaphysics with new world's mechanics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:50:31-07:00","id":609617,"title":"","content":"A little disappointed this is announced right after I bought a bunch of V20 books. I wonder how much of a departure it will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:53:35-07:00","id":609620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OrionTyson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609613#post609613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would like it if they published a proper game that was old universe and metaphysics with new world's mechanics</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I seriously wonder if that's the plan. It seems quite possible.<br /> <br /> At very least, with a new edition not restrained by &quot;nostalgia value&quot; like V20 was, expect them to move away from &quot;multiple actions&quot; as a mechanical thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:57:13-07:00","id":609649,"title":"","content":"Anything else announced? Any new V20 sourcebooks before V4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:11:27-07:00","id":609666,"title":"","content":"What ever happened to V20 Ghouls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:20:17-07:00","id":609698,"title":"","content":"I am excited, more excited than I should be about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7107-nachtal","name":"Nachtal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:24:03-07:00","id":609707,"title":"","content":"I am OK with this if it means more frequent releases, new clanbooks, etc. A total relaunch with proper backing and not a labor of love reliant solely on kickstarters. New clan books, sect guides, better crossover balancing, etc. Improvements used for nWoD but with CWoD metaplot and themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:31:03-07:00","id":609722,"title":"","content":"Hoping they update it to at least get rid of the multiple actions and varying target numbers. But otherwise I'm excited, although I'd rather they focused on the lines without a 20th Anniversary update released or in the works, if only because it would allow games like Demon to get the same support.<br /> <br /> I'm really hoping for the system to be brought closer to revised Storyteller though and for some changes to the setting (like having Roads instead of making all Vampires follow humanity), and for them to keep V20 as the 'classic' edition while 4e uses a more modern ruleset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:53:06-07:00","id":609746,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Grats to OP for finally talking CCP into letting you guys do a Fourth Edition!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m optimistic about the idea of a proper Fourth Edition. The X20s are cool, but there is always that hint of nostalgia; there were system tweaks, but never major overhauls. I\u2019m hoping that\u2019s what we get; a major system overhaul (like turning a VW Bug into a T81 Interceptor) but keeping all that juicy juicy metaplot drama. Granted, I end up ignoring half of it, but it was still fun to read about. ^_^<br /> <br /> Question that might invoke a deluge of hate:<br /> How would players feel if VtM4th had a system overhaul that is closer to the NWoD\u2019s system?<br /> </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:08:57-07:00","id":609770,"title":"","content":"I really, really hope they break with the previous tradition of &quot;the same game, jumped forward/backward a few years in time&quot; thing. They could really <i>revise</i> things and actually change up the mechanics. Fix a bunch of really old problems, clean up the Disciplines, clarify how Actions work, basically learn from the last 20 years of game development instead of just doing &quot;the same thing, but slightly tweaked&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:19:49-07:00","id":609778,"title":"","content":"My hope is the level of difference between the old editions and this new 4th edition is the same as the difference between first ed requiem and 2nd ed requiem.<br /> <br /> Cause that edition is the bomb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:20:18-07:00","id":609780,"title":"","content":"If they revise the dice mechanics with an actual probabilistic analysis, I'll scream like a little girl. I love the system as it is, but sometimes I'd just like it to be consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5246-warlock","name":"Warlock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:24:24-07:00","id":609784,"title":"","content":"I really, really hope they aren't moving toward the nWoD system, especially the 2.0 update. For all the talk of streamlining, nWoD's mechanics are a painful mess for someone who cares more about story then rules. This is why I prefer having cWoD rules separate. Some people like their WoD more like d20. I don't happen to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5525-rebelwithoutaclan","name":"RebelWithoutAClan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5525_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:45:23-07:00","id":609794,"title":"","content":"Okay first off...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://33.media.tumblr.com/ec86abb440176d257e51b0e3f9cda54a/tumblr_inline_mhy102BTQg1qz4rgp.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Now that that's out of the way, I too would like to see a mechanical improvement akin to what we've seen with 2E VtR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:48:04-07:00","id":609795,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm... okay. When they announced a new DA core, my reaction was that I was thrilled to see DA making a comeback, but V20 already had rules for the DA clans, so why did we need a new core? Couldn't they concentrate on setting material instead? I changed my mind, having been won over by the quality of the new and revised material that they included in DA20.<br /> <br /> So my first reaction to this - &quot;why do we need a new core when we already have V20?&quot;, is subject to change. But I'm curious as to why they think a new edition is needed. What are they planning to do in VtM4 that's different from V20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:50:29-07:00","id":609797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RebelWithoutAClan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609784#post609784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really, really hope they aren't moving toward the nWoD system, especially the 2.0 update. For all the talk of streamlining, nWoD's mechanics are a painful mess for someone who cares more about story then rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I haven't played 2nd Edition Requiem yet, but all the rule updates I've seen have been pretty damn solid, and when Blood &amp; Smoke came out, I heard almost universal praise. What mechanics in 2nd Ed are a painful mess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:58:22-07:00","id":609804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609795#post609795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious as to why they think a new edition is needed. What are they planning to do in VtM4 that's different from V20?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably more mechanical updates than they could do within the scope of V20 -- which was, after all, a commemorative edition that was never meant to revise the mechanics beyond simple polishing.<br /> <br /> I think the designers of VtM4 could do a lot worse than listen to Telgar, who has a solid grasp on how game mechanics should work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:06:56-07:00","id":609811,"title":"","content":"I don't know, something about trying to get the old setting up and running again seems...incorrect. The cWoD was all about the impending apocalypses, and since we actually got those it seems weird to keep moving forward with it (Not that the apocalypses we got we all that great). Plus, the entire point of the old system ending was because the well had run dry, and the metaplot had stretched things to their limit. Not to mention after ten or so years a lot of the flaws in the setting had become too huge to ignore and too ingrained to alter.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> That being said, a 4th Edition could work, so long as Onyx Path used it as a chance to overhaul a lot of the shortcomings, both mechanical (multiple actions, ugh!) and lore-based. I for one would like to see the Followers of Set expanded, tweaking their lore enough to give people greater room to play Setites that want nothing to do with their cult. Reorder the whole Giovanni/Cappadocian debacle so the Cappadocians are allowed to be a clan in the modern day, while still allowing the Giovanni to be running around.<br /> <br /> You know, alter the setting so it has a coherent history. Many of the growing pains VtM experienced were directly a result of the original designers 1) having no series bible, and 2) working from a specifically European/American mindset. Meaning a lot of the history of the Clans was determined retroactively to justify the current state of affairs, and the vampiric political landscape was uneven, and pulled from broad stereotypes. Then there's the fact that the Vampire splat was developed largely independently of the Werewolf splat and the Mage splat and the Changeling splat, etc. Good in the sense that they could all stand on their own without confusing entanglements, but bad in that it made it seem like the cWoD was in fact several separate, disconnected worlds. I'd like to see Onyx Path take all the elements of the CWoD and establish a concrete history from the ground up. How different clans interact with all others, how different regions of the world interact with the others, and how vampires as a whole interact with other supernaturals.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:07:14-07:00","id":609813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609746#post609746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Grats to OP for finally talking CCP into letting you guys do a Fourth Edition!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m optimistic about the idea of a proper Fourth Edition. The X20s are cool, but there is always that hint of nostalgia; there were system tweaks, but never major overhauls. I\u2019m hoping that\u2019s what we get; a major system overhaul (like turning a VW Bug into a T81 Interceptor) but keeping all that juicy juicy metaplot drama. Granted, I end up ignoring half of it, but it was still fun to read about. ^_^<br /> <br /> Question that might invoke a deluge of hate:<br /> How would players feel if VtM4th had a system overhaul that is closer to the NWoD\u2019s system?<br /> </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Making 4th editions use Storytelling instead of an overhauled Storyteller would cut into the translation guides' collective territory. Given that, I'm guessing that it's not an option that's going to be on the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:31:19-07:00","id":609829,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there'll be plenty of changes to Disciplines and other rules elements, but I'm not betting any money just yet on a total system overhaul.* I mean, White Wolf already did that eleven years ago! The result is the NWoD. Then you have the whole issues of mechanical incompatibility with earlier products, wanting to keep the CWoD lines distinct from the NWoD lines (all the better to attract fans of the former who aren't into the latter), and the question of whether M20, C20 and the W20s should get similar overhauls...<br /> <br /> ...but hey, what do I know! I don't know what OPP is planning. Beyond that it's going to be ten kinds of awesome, and that I am positively gleeful at the thought of forking over my hard-earned dollars to them. How soon until the Kickstarter!?<br /> <br /> * (Although as a guy who runs his VtM games using NWoD/VtR 2e rules... I can dream...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:32:44-07:00","id":609830,"title":"","content":"What?<br /> <br /> I mean, ok, I have only a basic familiarity with the cWoD, but...<br /> <br /> For Real? Freakin' For Real?<br /> <br /> This <i><u>Just</u></i> got a new edition. They spent 4+ years establishing and releasing products for this framework, to revitalize all these old but very popular games...<br /> <br /> And now that's just being swept out for something newer? What?<br /> <br /> I saw something similar a number of times. The most prominent I remember was when DnD 4th was replaced in three years by its Essentials remodeling. After an initial wave of products, the line petered out in about a year and a half, replaced again in a few more years by 5th. And sure, some said they were addressing valid complaints, and besides, the Onyx Path crew are very competent. But they are still producing new content for the 20thA. Lore of the Clans and Bloodlines are still in progress. New products have just been announced alongside this new edition for the existing revitalization.<br /> <br /> VtM has always been a favorite, and using it as a focus for launching initiatives like editions and outlier products (board/card/video games) is a sound choice, but this feels like an oversaturation. Sure, older editions were released on a similar scale, but given the structure of Onyx Path today, and all their other lines, it seems to be more of a lateral, if not detrimental, move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3708-amateur-hour","name":"Amateur Hour","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:33:44-07:00","id":609832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609811#post609811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I for one would like to see the Followers of Set expanded, tweaking their lore enough to give people greater room to play Setites that want nothing to do with their cult. Reorder the whole Giovanni/Cappadocian debacle so the Cappadocians are allowed to be a clan in the modern day, while still allowing the Giovanni to be running around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like I'm not the only one that objects to the Followers of Set. Personally I think their overtly cartoonish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6752-jeebers76","name":"Jeebers76","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:42:59-07:00","id":609840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amateur Hour</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609830#post609830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What?<br /> <br /> I mean, ok, I have only a basic familiarity with the cWoD, but...<br /> <br /> For Real? Freakin' For Real?<br /> <br /> This <i><u>Just</u></i> got a new edition. They spent 4+ years establishing and releasing products for this framework, to revitalize all these old but very popular games...<br /> <br /> And now that's just being swept out for something newer? What?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spaceballs said it best: It's the Search For More Money.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6752-jeebers76","name":"Jeebers76","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:46:04-07:00","id":609846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeebers76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609840#post609840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spaceballs said it best: It's the Search For More Money.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. No one who works for the tabletop RPG industry, much less for a company as small as OPP, is doing it because they hope to make oodles of cash. How many employees other than Rich even hold full-time jobs at OPP again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:54:08-07:00","id":609852,"title":"","content":"You don't have to be rich to want more money. It just makes it easier to get. Greed is a simple motivator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6752-jeebers76","name":"Jeebers76","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:55:33-07:00","id":609853,"title":"","content":"Frankly, a lot of the original WoD material is pretty offensive on some levels - Vampire's &quot;racist-stereotype based secondary Clans&quot; always really irked me, and Werewolf was even worse for that. They tried to smooth off the edge on that kind of thing over time, and they avoided those pitfalls entirely with NWoD for the most part, but I know with the X20 editions they were chained by producing essentially a nostalgia driven product. They couldn't go back and really edit too much of that stuff too hard.<br /> <br /> I think a 4th edition would be an opportunity to really aggressively go after a lot of that stuff and fix it up to make it fit better with 2015 sensibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:03:20-07:00","id":609854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeebers76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609852#post609852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to be rich to want more money. It just makes it easier to get. Greed is a simple motivator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but most greedy people are looking to get <i>more</i> money than they get now. And the steps towards more money generally start at:<br /> <i>1.) Leave the RPG industry and find a business that isn't held aloft mostly by self-exploitation of all people involved.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:22:36-07:00","id":609866,"title":"","content":"This is really unexpected. I love what's been done with V20, but a new, unjaundiced revamping of VtM, with the same care that's been taken with the nWoD second editions? That's something I could really get behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:29:04-07:00","id":609872,"title":"","content":"I can get behind Demon the Fallen Revised. Hope V4 succeeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:29:09-07:00","id":609873,"title":"","content":"I played a lot of V:tM (Revised Edition) in college and recently came back to the game after getting some friends hooked on the idea. In the past couple of months I have spent quite a lot of money on source material, including but not limited to the premium colour version of V20 as well as all of the clanbooks and &quot;guide to&quot; books, so that I could learn the game again and run my own whilst also playing in a game run by a friend. I could well have simply downloaded the PDFs illicitly, but I wanted to build a nice collection and help Onyx Path make some money as a &quot;thank you&quot; for continuing to print the materials and write new ones.<br /> <br /> To echo the sentiment of many here I'm not sure this will be of any interest to me, with some caveats.<br /> <br /> I basically have two criteria that would make me even consider trading up:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">This edition must be suitably distinct from V20.<br /> This edition must be substantially better.*</div><span style=\"font-size:9px\">*Hopefully without sacrificing the depth that kept many of us with V:tM instead of moving on to V:tR. Fixing needlessly complicated mechanics would be fine, if it were to remove <i>tedium</i> as opposed to <i>depth</i>.</span><br /> <br /> As others have already suggested also, a part of me is concerned this might essentially be an official NWoD port of V:tM, in which case I have zero interest.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I guess the worst case scenario for me is that I have built up a nice collection for V20, a game I thoroughly enjoy playing and will hopefully get to play for many years to come. In which case I should just consider it money well spent and carry on enjoying myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 07-31-2015, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:33:26-07:00","id":609886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeebers76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609852#post609852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to be rich to want more money. It just makes it easier to get. Greed is a simple motivator.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, when pointed out in this context it usually betrays a lack of knowledge of how making money in the RPG industry actually works.<br /> <br /> If a RPG company wants to maximize profits, they milk an existing edition as long as possible. Supplements have far less costs to create, thus they can make more of them and generate more sales. New editions and new core books are a huge investment of time, money, and resources. If OPP and CCP intended to simply make more money, they'd continue on the 20th edition bandwagon without announcing an official 4th edition for much, much longer. The 20ths books have generally been well received, are selling well, and there's clear demand for more of them.<br /> <br /> This announcement actually risks money, because it generates consumer fear that buying 20th books is pointless because in a few years 4e will come out and there'll be a whole new set of books to buy all over again. There's a major risk that the timing will result in resentment towards 4e and reduce profits.<br /> <br /> Understanding how RPGs generate money is important to understanding what's really a &quot;money grab&quot; and what's not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:42:13-07:00","id":609894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OrionTyson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609613#post609613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would like it if they published a proper game that was old universe and metaphysics with new world's mechanics</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Ii'd like it. While the nWoD's mechanics are mostly nice (Awakening's mechanics are gorgeous), they're geared toward accomplishing less impressive feats that what is usual in the cWoD, and its character creation system is in my opinon stricly inferior (Where are my bonus points people? WHERE?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T13:45:48-07:00","id":609896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeebers76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609840#post609840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spaceballs said it best: It's the Search For More Money.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it. If you just wanted to make money, &quot;quit working in tabletop RPGs&quot; would be point one on your Master Plan (TM). No, they have some kind of vision about where they want to take VtM. I just wonder what it is, and why it needs a new core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:00:52-07:00","id":609918,"title":"","content":"Well for me I really also liked the V20 stuff. But I already own all the previous books. Much of the v20 stuff was a reprinting of a lot of the stuff in the old books.<br /> <br /> Which is great for a fan getting back into it or a new fan. But for someone like me...I still had all this stuff.<br /> <br /> Of course there was new stuff here and there but a lot of was just reprints of old stuff.<br /> <br /> Again nothing wrong with that at all and I own all the v20 stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T14:13:15-07:00","id":609927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609918#post609918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well for me I really also liked the V20 stuff. But I already own all the previous books. Much of the v20 stuff was a reprinting of a lot of the stuff in the old books.<br /> <br /> Which is great for a fan getting back into it or a new fan. But for someone like me...I still had all this stuff.<br /> <br /> Of course there was new stuff here and there but a lot of was just reprints of old stuff.<br /> <br /> Again nothing wrong with that at all and I own all the v20 stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and No. There wasn't a huge amount in V20 that was truly new, I agree, although a few things were tweaked and improved. What I liked about it was that it had the depth of background of the later editions - all the clans and sects fleshed out, for instance - but setting-wise, pretty much reverted it to second edition, before they launched a metaplot to destroy the world, so the whole &quot;these are the Final Nights&quot; riff didn't reverberate through everything anyone said or did. That was ideal for me, just what I was looking for. Plus, the original books were 90s or early 2000s, and it was great to see the cWoD get an update to the present decade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:32:49-07:00","id":610034,"title":"","content":"Seriously ?!!?! <br /> Now, the question is <b><i>WHAT</i></b> will it be ?<br /> A rule overhaul ?<br /> A new metaplot base (as Rich said one Monday Note, the Metaplot is what follows) ?<br /> A complete revision of the Clan/Sect/Path/Bloodline/Whatever ?<br /> <br /> Probably the first one, possibly the second one (as some of the recent V20 book advanced some plot points, and that would give space to grow the setting/change things to keep things &quot;interesting&quot;). the third one... really, they cannot change a Clan without alienating some of the base. They cant change some aspect of the setting and still call it &quot;Vampire : the Masquerade&quot; Minor change (like the Kyasid in VDA 20), yes, but remove a Clan or irrevocally alter some aspect, I don't think so.<br /> And the fact is that there is some V20 product on the way, they can't just annonce a new edition and then say : &quot;Oh, and the next year or so of books won't be compatible&quot;<br /> <br /> BTW, did Rich said who will develop it ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:46:56-07:00","id":610041,"title":"","content":"I know this isn't a popular opinion, but screw it, I love metaplot, and I'll be happy to see it progress in some form. I don't know why so many ST's and players can't cope with the concept that they are free to use what they want from it.<br /> <br /> Hoping for a good rules overhaul and better discipline balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:47:03-07:00","id":610042,"title":"","content":"I am cautiously intrigued. I <i>have </i>V20, and I've fiddled with it and ironed out all the quirks so it runs perfectly for me and my troupe. The metaplot does not interest me; if this new edition pushes it too hard, I'd hesitate to pick it up. Perhaps this is an opportunity to rebuild from the ground up, rather than play to the nostalgia like V20 did/does, and I'd be happy to see a more objective/critical outlining of the Clans and such, but if all this new edition does is clean up the writing for Vicissitude so people stop complaining about it, then it's not for me. I agree with DarkwaveDomina when she said<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkwaveDomina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609873#post609873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This edition must be suitably distinct from V20.<br /> This edition must be substantially better.</div> </div> </div> </div>And really, with new models of business and distribution, I was really hoping to see the &quot;supplement/printing treadmill&quot; disappear. Ah, well, nothing's perfect.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:09:44-07:00","id":610065,"title":"","content":"Here's hoping for a massive overhaul that makes all the old fans angry!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:22:37-07:00","id":610077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amateur Hour</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609830#post609830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What?<br /> <br /> I mean, ok, I have only a basic familiarity with the cWoD, but...<br /> <br /> For Real? Freakin' For Real?<br /> <br /> This <i><u>Just</u></i> got a new edition. They spent 4+ years establishing and releasing products for this framework, to revitalize all these old but very popular games...<br /> <br /> And now that's just being swept out for something newer? What?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put money on a table that this is what happened (as it's what happened with the New World of Darkness and the &quot;Chronicle&quot; books being replaced by 2nd Edition books): Onyx Path wanted to do a new edition from day one. CCP said &quot;no&quot; - they wanted to sell the nostalgia value for the old lines rather than do an overhaul. NOW (possibly due to OP success... or maybe due to the plans for the MMO being dropped and so CCP has less riding on a particular model of the gamelines) they've approved the new edition with the full overhaul Onyx Path wanted to do the whole time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-31-2015, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:43:14-07:00","id":610111,"title":"","content":"Ok, before we get excited (or not), is this even official? I mean, they will release this new edition for sure or it's like the cWOD MMO PC game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:44:05-07:00","id":610112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610065#post610065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's hoping for a massive overhaul that makes all the old fans angry!</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll just stick with V20 though. q:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:45:24-07:00","id":610114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610077#post610077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd put money on a table that this is what happened (as it's what happened with the New World of Darkness and the &quot;Chronicle&quot; books being replaced by 2nd Edition books): Onyx Path wanted to do a new edition from day one. CCP said &quot;no&quot; - they wanted to sell the nostalgia value for the old lines rather than do an overhaul. NOW (possibly due to OP success... or maybe due to the plans for the MMO being dropped and so CCP has less riding on a particular model of the gamelines) they've approved the new edition with the full overhaul Onyx Path wanted to do the whole time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\">To quote Christoph Waltz: &quot;That's a Bingo!&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd aslo bet hard-earned oboli that's the crux of the announcement.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:08:23-07:00","id":610150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610065#post610065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's hoping for a massive overhaul that makes all the old fans angry!</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry. Twitter, Facebook, and RPG.net already are setting camps for the oncoming flame wars. People are using this target Vampire the Requiem and it has nothing to do with V4th.<br /> #OWoD<br /> #NWoD<br /> #LoveBoth.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:09:10-07:00","id":610161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609872#post609872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can get behind Demon the Fallen Revised. Hope V4 succeeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I support this fully.<br /> #DemonLove<br /> #LuciferRising","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:28:23-07:00","id":610180,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.<br /> I'm not going to start guessing too much. I'll be happy to wait until we're given some solid information.<br /> <br /> But I can't help but wonder what this means for the metaplot.<br /> Are we going to see another &quot;the end times haven't happened yet&quot; ala V20?<br /> A Revised Convention book take of &quot;It came. It went. Nothing special happened&quot;.<br /> Or, dare I say it a post-Gehenna setting of &quot;the world went to hell. This is what happened next&quot;?<br /> Interesting time to be a V:tM fan indeed.<br /> <br /> I'm just hoping we don't see any more bloody edition-bashing in the near future.<br /> It always makes me nauseous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:39:46-07:00","id":610190,"title":"","content":"I always wanted to run gehenna like how this was in angel.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.quotes.net/show-quote/4317\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.stands4.com/app_common/img/top_logo_quo.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.quotes.net/show-quote/4317\" target=\"_blank\"> Holland Manners: Congratulations. Great victory.Angel: You're...Holland: Holland Manners.Angel: ...not alive.Holland: Oh, no. I'm quite dead. [shows Angel the bite mark Darla left on his neck] Unfortunately my contract with Wolfram &amp; Hart extends well beyond that. [smiles] Hop on in. You certainly earned it.[Angel enters the elevator]Holland: Well, this is exciting, isn't it? Going straight to the source. So what's the big plan, Angel? Destroy the Senior Partners, smash Wolfram &amp; Hart once and for all?Angel: Something like that.Holland: Hmm, now tell me just what do you think that would accomplish? In the end, I mean.Angel: It'll be-the end.Holland: Well, the end of you, certainly. But I meant in the larger sense.Angel: In the larger sense, I really don't give a crap.Holland: Now, I don't think that's true. Be honest-you got the tiniest bit of \"give a crap\" left. Otherwise you wouldn't be going on this kamikaze mission. Now let me see, there was something in a sacred prophecy, some oblique reference to you. Something you're supposed to prevent. Now what was that?Angel: The apocalypse.Holland: Yes, the apocalypse, of course. Another one of those. Well, it's true, we do have one scheduled. And I imagine if you were to prevent it you would save a great many people. Well, you should do that then. Absolutely! I wasn't thinking. [smiles] Of course, all those people you save from that apocalypse would then have the next one to look forward to, but hey, it's always something, isn't it?Angel: You're not gonna win.Holland: Well...no. Of course we aren't. We have no intention of doing anything so prosaic as \"winning\". [laughs]Angel: Then why?Holland: Hmm? I'm sorry, why what?Angel: Why fight?Holland: That's really the question you should be asking yourself, isn't it? See, for us, there is no fight. Which is why winning doesn't enter into it. We...go on, no matter what. Our firm has always been here...in one form or another. The Inquisition. The Khmer Rouge. We were there when the very first cave man clubbed his neighbor. See, we're in the hearts and minds of every single living being. And that, friend, is what's making things so difficult for you. See, the world doesn't work in spite of evil, Angel. It works with us. It works because of us.[elevator comes to a stop and the doors open, revealing Los Angeles]Holland: Welcome to the home office.Angel: This isn't...Holland: Oh, you know it is. You know that better than anyone. Things you've seen. Things you've-well, done. You see, if there wasn't evil in every single one of them out there-why, they wouldn't be people. They'd all be angels.[Angel slowly walks out of the elevator]Holland: Have a nice day. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.quotes.net/show-quote/4317\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.quotes.net/show-quote/4317 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A great memorable quote from the Angel, Season 2 show on Quotes.net </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The idea that the apoclypse is now. The world of darkness is an awful place...who ever said the end would be a big bang? <br /> <br /> I find much more horror in the idea that the end times are subtle in how awful the world is. LIke the antideluvians have been awake and active for centuries. Manipulating the entire world to be as awful as it is from the shadows.<br /> <br /> Whoever said it would be some big battle?<br /> <br /> That is my gehenna :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:56:12-07:00","id":610203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610077#post610077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd put money on a table that this is what happened (as it's what happened with the New World of Darkness and the &quot;Chronicle&quot; books being replaced by 2nd Edition books): Onyx Path wanted to do a new edition from day one. CCP said &quot;no&quot; - they wanted to sell the nostalgia value for the old lines rather than do an overhaul. NOW (possibly due to OP success... or maybe due to the plans for the MMO being dropped and so CCP has less riding on a particular model of the gamelines) they've approved the new edition with the full overhaul Onyx Path wanted to do the whole time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I somewhat doubt this is the case.<br /> <br /> V20 happened before Onyx Path did. I think the safer bet is that Onyx Path wasn't initially expecting the cWOD books to become as important to their line-up as they have. They probably were completely on board with just doing the 20th books at first, and didn't really decided to look at a new cWOD edition until after the original five White Wolf cWOD books got their anniversary editions into the works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:09:22-07:00","id":610209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andreas Rayne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610180#post610180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm.<br /> I'm not going to start guessing too much. I'll be happy to wait until we're given some solid information.<br /> <br /> But I can't help but wonder what this means for the metaplot.<br /> Are we going to see another &quot;the end times haven't happened yet&quot; ala V20?<br /> A Revised Convention book take of &quot;It came. It went. Nothing special happened&quot;.<br /> Or, dare I say it a post-Gehenna setting of &quot;the world went to hell. This is what happened next&quot;?<br /> Interesting time to be a V:tM fan indeed.<br /> <br /> I'm just hoping we don't see any more bloody edition-bashing in the near future.<br /> It always makes me nauseous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of people either forgot or didn't know that OPP is putting out an metaplot book &quot;Beckett's Diary&quot;. I wonder if it will tie into V4th or not. Same with Lore of the Clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:21:02-07:00","id":610310,"title":"","content":"I talked to Eddy about this for a few minutes at their booth. It's not going to be NWoD. To paraphrase, he wants Vampire to be as cutting edge a roleplaying game as it was when it first launched. That means looking at how our hobby has evolved and cracking open the VtM mechanics to see if things can just be done better. If I her a chance I'll ask about setting stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:28:48-07:00","id":610315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moogle001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610310#post610310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I talked to Eddy about this for a few minutes at their booth. It's not going to be NWoD. To paraphrase, he wants Vampire to be as cutting edge a roleplaying game as it was when it first launched. That means looking at how our hobby has evolved and cracking open the VtM mechanics to see if things can just be done better.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much exactly what I was hoping for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:37:58-07:00","id":610319,"title":"","content":"I've got my fingers crossed that there'll be no sacred cows in this, that the team takes a hard look at all the excess (and problematic!) stuff that's been grandfathered in simply on account of bing old. <br /> <br /> (I mostly want to Giovanni and Setites to get big fat revisions, and for there to be explicit DON'T BE ASSHOLES sidebars of the Ravnos and Malkavian sections).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:57:33-07:00","id":610327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610319#post610319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got my fingers crossed that there'll be no sacred cows in this, that the team takes a hard look at all the excess (and problematic!) stuff that's been grandfathered in simply on account of bing old.<br /> <br /> (I mostly want to Giovanni and Setites to get big fat revisions, and for there to be explicit DON'T BE ASSHOLES sidebars of the Ravnos and Malkavian sections).</div> </div> </div> </div>Caine himself could give that mandate and someone will still try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T22:17:12-07:00","id":610415,"title":"","content":"Not too excited by this news. I've bought into all the 20th Anniversary books so far, and now we are getting a new edition without the current &quot;edition&quot; even being finished. DA 20 and Mage 20 have pretty good versions of the cWoD rules. <br /> Once all the 20th Anniversary games are out, I really have no desire to buy all the products again so soon.<br /> <br /> I was really hoping this announcement just meant that V20 (as the least updated 20th product) was getting the polish it deserved. Instead it has me wondering if I should invest in any more 20th products. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T23:49:30-07:00","id":610506,"title":"","content":"In regards to all the metaplot question, OPP should just do what they did with M20 - have 'Future Fates' allowing you to decides what happened and what didn't. We will anyway - who could argue with that as an approach?<br /> <br /> However my big question is HOW is this the fourth edition? Revised was 3rd, V20 was fourth. I am spinning out here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7114-dreamsreign","name":"DreamsReign","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T00:01:43-07:00","id":610510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moogle001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610310#post610310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I talked to Eddy about this for a few minutes at their booth. It's not going to be NWoD. To paraphrase, he wants Vampire to be as cutting edge a roleplaying game as it was when it first launched. That means looking at how our hobby has evolved and cracking open the VtM mechanics to see if things can just be done better. If I her a chance I'll ask about setting stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's interesting, because based on what someone said during the V20 redevelopment, most &quot;mechanics-orientated&quot; fans tend to lean towards nWoD, whereas &quot;setting-orientated&quot; fans tend to lean towards cWoD. Personally, I think that's because cWoD simply has a much richer and more fully realized background. But I'm not sure that streamlining the mechanics on its own will necessarily be a big seller for the old-school fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T00:12:52-07:00","id":610516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610510#post610510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's interesting, because based on what someone said during the V20 redevelopment, most &quot;mechanics-orientated&quot; fans tend to lean towards nWoD, whereas &quot;setting-orientated&quot; fans tend to lean towards cWoD. Personally, I think that's because cWoD simply has a much richer and more fully realized background. But I'm not sure that streamlining the mechanics on its own will necessarily be a big seller for the old-school fans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As one who has been playing white-wolf since '94, I have no problem with some rules getting a polish and crystal clear clarification... so long as they don't throw the baby out with the bathwater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T00:54:28-07:00","id":610525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DreamsReign</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610506#post610506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However my big question is HOW is this the fourth edition? Revised was 3rd, V20 was fourth. I am spinning out here.</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 was billed as a &quot;nostalgia omnibus&quot; edition by the White Wolf arm of CCP, more of a 3.5 than a full, though the other lines (W20, M20) under Onyx Path took the opportunity to do some larger overhauls. Seeing some of the changes made by subsequent publications, DAV20 in particular (M20 in extremis), V20 really comes off as a half-step in revision.<br /> <br /> This has been a complaint since the early days of White Wolf; since <i>Vampire </i>was/is usually published first, the other game lines streamline and focus things presented in it, so in essence <i>Vampire Revised</i> built off <i>Werewolf</i>/<i>Mage</i>/<i>Changeling</i>/<i>Wraith 2e </i>and mechanically operated more like them than the rest of the Revised line. It's the burden of the first-born.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T00:55:28-07:00","id":610527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610516#post610516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As one who has been playing white-wolf since '94, I have no problem with some rules getting a polish and crystal clear clarification... so long as they don't throw the baby out with the bathwater.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but a polish and crystal clear explanation is what we should be getting in the 20th books. I don't really want a whole new &quot;edition&quot; for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T02:16:22-07:00","id":610574,"title":"","content":"I personally don't like this. Especially if they try to update the other 20th lines to a 4th too, given they WERE more fully updated than vamp. Even so, I feel like this isn't needed, myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:57:46-07:00","id":610645,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda pissed about this. I feel like I got ripped off for V20 now, let alone the companion, Hunter's Hunted 2nd edition, Anarch's Unbound and Blood Magic... Seriously, is there even a fucking point to me purchasing the Black Hand Book and Lore of the Clans now?<br /> <br /> Isn't that all just going to be invalidated by V:tM 4th?<br /> <br /> Should I put off buying anymore 20th anniversary books now period, since they're just going to be replaced by 4th edition books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T04:31:56-07:00","id":610655,"title":"","content":"I kinda see both sides of this.<br /> <br /> V20 was the first new CWoD book in ten years, it was also meant to be a stand-alone, as far as I know. It is pretty much purely a anniversary edition book, and I can understand the writers wanting to actually do changes proper.<br /> <br /> But I think it might be a bit too soon, we've still got books getting released for V20 that serve the purpose of updating the setting. That, and after V20, each Anniversary ed has been more like an edition, with Wraith and Changeling basically getting entirely remade.<br /> <br /> If V20 books will be counted as 4th ed books, I think that would ease a lot of people's minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T04:42:09-07:00","id":610663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610645#post610645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda pissed about this. I feel like I got ripped off for V20 now, let alone the companion, Hunter's Hunted 2nd edition, Anarch's Unbound and Blood Magic... Seriously, is there even a fucking point to me purchasing the Black Hand Book and Lore of the Clans now?<br /> <br /> Isn't that all just going to be invalidated by V:tM 4th?<br /> <br /> Should I put off buying anymore 20th anniversary books now period, since they're just going to be replaced by 4th edition books?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much exactly how I'm feeling at this point.<br /> I've been waiting forever for Lore of the Clans, and now before I get it a new edition is announced!?<br /> Kind of ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T04:54:45-07:00","id":610668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610655#post610655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If V20 books will be counted as 4th ed books, I think that would ease a lot of people's minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. I don't want the new books to change the setting or remove so called &quot;Problematic elements from V20&quot;...it will pretty much mean there's no reason to buy the upcoming books if we're getting massive setting overhauls..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T05:20:20-07:00","id":610686,"title":"","content":"More info on Vampire: The Masquerade 4th Edition via Reddit and Ian Watson from OPP (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/3fayio/vtm_4th_edition_announced_for):\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRP...nnounced_for):</a><br /> <br /> \u00abI know people want clarification when we do a big announcement like this, but &quot;while the staff is all at Gen Con&quot; is not the time to demand it -- and yes, we have had many demands. We're working like 12-15 hours a day for a week. Someone else already pointed out my Tweet where I said a full blog post explaining everything (probably from Rich or Eddy) will be posted once we get back from Gen Con.<br /> <br /> That said I'll try to hit a few of the high notes:<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> It's been 18 years since the last edition. We've always maintained that V20 was not a &quot;new edition,&quot; but rather an &quot;anniversary edition&quot; (or &quot;nostalgia edition&quot;). VTM1, VTM2, and VTM Revised were each distinct steps forward. V20 looked back on those steps appreciatively, and allowed us to revisit them. VTM4 is a step forward. If you're happy with V20, great! No one's forcing you, or has ever forced you, to change editions. We've made a ton of amazing V20 products. V20 was a toolkit that let you play the Vampire you liked best, so if you still like V20 best, more power to you!<br /> <br /> It's too soon!<br /> People seem to have a magic number in their heads for a right amount of time between editions, but it always either seems to fall in &quot;too soon&quot; or &quot;too long&quot; with very few people ever feeling satisfied that it's coming out at just the right time. 2011 was the 20th anniversary of VTM. 2016 is the 25th anniversary. There was only one year between VTM1 (1991) and VTM2 (1992). There was six years between VTM2 and Revised (1998). Even counting from V20, five years is plenty of time between editions.<br /> <br /> Why now, before Wraith20 and Changeling20 are done?<br /> Vampire 2e was out before Mage (and Wraith, and Changeling)'s first editions were released. The CWoD's first two editions continued a tradition of releasing a 2e of each game two years after the first edition was released, regardless of where that fell in the development of other game lines. Overlapping editions has been a thing since the early days. This is nothing new. It's right for VTM4 to happen now, so that's what we're doing. That doesn't prevent other games from getting the X20 editions they deserve, and they will.<br /> <br /> This is a cash grab.<br /> If that's what we wanted to do, this is the worst industry in which to do it. However much money you think we'd be making on this, you're probably being extremely generous with your guesses.<br /> <br /> What about V20 supplements?<br /> We'll be finishing off the announced V20 supplements. Since V20 supplements by their very design are supposed to be metaplot-agnostic, I don't see why they'd suddenly be completely useless with VTM4 around the corner.<br /> <br /> Is this a rebrand of V20?<br /> No. V20's default assumption is that Gehenna is still a nebulous possibility (probability?) which may happen in the future. VTM4 follows directly from Revised: Gehenna (or something like it) happened 12 years ago. Where does that leave Kindred society now?<br /> <br /> One of the things Eddy and Rich told me was that V20, although it was set in a nebulous &quot;now,&quot; was still very much a 20th century game (you might even be more specific and say it was a '90s game). It was a present from the creators to the fans, designed to instill nostalgia of the first three editions.<br /> <br /> VTM4 is being made as a Vampire for the 21st century. What does that mean? How will that look? That's what we'll be working out over the next year, with input from the fanbase. Eddy has a strong vision of what he wants, but as always, getting fan feedback is an important part of our process.<br /> <br /> Whether you're excited about the prospect or you don't see the point, I hope you'll at least give us some benefit of the doubt and help give us your input via open development on the road to VTM4 over the next year. Maybe you'll see something you like.<br /> <br /> I'm sure many of you will be tempted to respond to this with more questions or vociferous rebuttals or whatever, but as I said, a comprehensive blog post is coming very soon. Please have patience. I'm not going to involve myself further in this until then, because A) it's not my game and B) I'm still at Gen Con and I'm tired.<br /> <br /> Now I'm going to bed; I have a Trinity panel in the morning.\u00bb","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/49-jrmariano","name":"jrmariano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar49_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T05:26:15-07:00","id":610697,"title":"","content":"Wow, well I guess I won't be bothering to purchase anymore 20th anniversary stuff from Onyx Path. Best to just wait for the new editions and not waste my money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T05:46:38-07:00","id":610706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610697#post610697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, well I guess I won't be bothering to purchase anymore 20th anniversary stuff from Onyx Path. Best to just wait for the new editions and not waste my money.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you feel that way Orphan.<br /> I for one will continue to buy V20 products because 1) I'm a completionist and 2) I think Ian's response made it pretty clear that 4th Ed will be an entirely different animal to V20.<br /> This edition is obviously not going to be retreading old ground.<br /> <br /> Also, can I say my previous post was spot on with it's setting?<br /> No? Well I already have done!<br /> Yay me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T05:57:54-07:00","id":610710,"title":"","content":"Well I dont care just bring Moncada back.....GLORIOUS!!!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7120-phelios","name":"Phelios","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:03:51-07:00","id":610712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jrmariano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610686#post610686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VTM4 follows directly from Revised: Gehenna (or something like it) happened 12 years ago. Where does that leave Kindred society now?</div> </div> </div> </div>WHAT? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That makes even less sense. If Gehenna happening in 2004 is cannon, then I don't see how the game line is viable at all. We either have no vampires at all, or we have mostly neonates who know nothing about the decades of backstory (thus,rendering it moot) and end up with a Requiem-like situation...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jrmariano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610686#post610686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope you'll at least give us some benefit of the doubt and help give us your input via open development on the road to VTM4 over the next year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actuall, no. Not after what you have done with VtR 2.0. The nWoD 2.0 clearly shows that people with a good grip on game design have left the building. I don't see OPP without someone like Justin Achilles in any shape to produce new rules. If you get him on board, I am in. But if mediocre designers like David Hill are allowed to take the helm on this, I am out. My confidence in OPP producing quality rules and quality games are at an all-time low.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:14:34-07:00","id":610724,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Personal attacks are against forum rules.. Darksider.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 08-02-2015, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6752-jeebers76","name":"Jeebers76","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:15:44-07:00","id":610725,"title":"","content":"This really is starting to sound like it's more &quot;World of Darkness Part III&quot; rather than a continuation of Masquerade... I mean if you're going to say Gehenna happened just so you can wildly change the setting and write up entirely new rules...Why not just make a NewNwod Vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:18:13-07:00","id":610727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jrmariano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610686#post610686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20's default assumption is that Gehenna is still a nebulous possibility (probability?) which may happen in the future. VTM4 follows directly from Revised: Gehenna (or something like it) happened 12 years ago. Where does that leave Kindred society now?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is awesome. Totally awesome. I'm sold on V4e based on this alone. I love the idea of a massive shakeup like this - makes it clear that we're heading into new territory. Badass <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:19:28-07:00","id":610738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeebers76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610724#post610724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ich. I can't stand Justin Achilles' terrible writing skills! He was an okay developer but he couldn't write for (bleep)! New York by Night and the two Giovanni clanbooks plus the Giovanni clan novel was his baby, and all sucked rocks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pair him with the current VtR 2.0 writers. Rose Bailey and her team are kickass at writing the setting parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:21:24-07:00","id":610743,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't understand the attack here Murder-of-Crows.<br /> <br /> There are certain books I like and others I don't - but there's also a gigantic catalog that you can pick and choose from.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I'll run VTM4, I haven't seen it yet, and we have a while to wait before open dev starts. If I don't like it then I'll stick with V20 and the supplements I bought for that (or VtM: The other editions). No one is going to take away those books from me or the enjoyment I get from them. Another edition doesn't change the stories I make in those worlds if my gaming group and I choose to ignore them (hell, I picked and chose only bits from any game I liked)<br /> <br /> As for NWoD, I wasn't overly keen on 1st Edition and really like how 2nd Edition is, but I know that others feel the other way around. That's fine, as I've said, there's a wealth of books out there to choose from. I wouldn't call the devs, or anyone involved &quot;mediocre&quot;. I have my own favorites, and I can reason why I don't like some others as much, but that's personal preference rather than the quality of their work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:22:21-07:00","id":610744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orphan81</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610697#post610697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, well I guess I won't be bothering to purchase anymore 20th anniversary stuff from Onyx Path. Best to just wait for the new editions and not waste my money.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why you'd assume every game line is going to get a &quot;4th&quot; edition or that it'll be any time soon. Heck, depending on Kick starter results we may not get a 20th book for each CWoD setting. But if you're confident that well see those books and can wait another decade for, say, Demon, by all means don't buy the 20th books.<br /> <br /> I fully appreciate why some people may hate this news, but we can probably all agree it is in the best interest of the game lines as products, and thus the communitiy as a whole. The 20th books are great, but what they are not is attractive to new people; I'm seriously questioning how I can get any of my players to read M20. Whether they're their own edition or not, the 20th books really are celebrations for longtime fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:22:30-07:00","id":610745,"title":"","content":"Just a thought: 11 years ago writing a post-Gehenna setting for a 4th edition Vampire: The Masquerade would have made a lot more sense - and would have avoided splitting the fanbase.<br /> <br /> (Also, yes, I personally start to see exciting opportunities in a post-Gehenna setting...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:28:39-07:00","id":610747,"title":"","content":"This still all seems really unnecessary. Just stick a weird post-Gehenna meta plot onto VtR 2.0 and call it good.<br /> <br /> I don't understand how this isn't supposed to feel like a kick in the balls to us cWoD fans still buying X20 material.<br /> <br /> (Plus, bringing in new players would just be weird. &quot;All this origin stuff happened, then the Vampire apocalypse happened, and now it's all new origin stuff. Make a character.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:35:47-07:00","id":610748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610747#post610747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This still all seems really unnecessary. Just stick a weird post-Gehenna meta plot onto VtR 2.0 and call it good.<br /> <br /> I don't understand how this isn't supposed to feel like a kick in the balls to us cWoD fans still buying X20 material.<br /> <br /> (Plus, bringing in new players would just be weird. &quot;All this origin stuff happened, then the Vampire apocalypse happened, and now it's all new origin stuff. Make a character.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanics are not the only differences between VtM and VtR by a long shot. As both products grow now, they'll probably diverge even more. Besides which, the NWoD rules aren't exactly revolutionary themselves. While I'm certain they keep the basics of the Storyteller system, there's plenty that can be adopted from indie RPG titles that would amplify the feel of VtM. That's what I'm hoping we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:35:54-07:00","id":610749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MeetsInTaverns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610743#post610743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I don't understand the attack here Murder-of-Crows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of pent-up nerd-rage about stuff like V20DA and VtR 2.0. Both are less than they could've been, to say it politely. Especially V20DA would have required a completely different developer. Thing is, V20DA is a complete failure at combing the best of the old and doing small updates to the rules and fluff. V20DA feels a lot like the developer having a field day changing stuff around to turn the WoD into &quot;his&quot; personal setting instead of honoring the great design work done in the past. And frankly, I am fed up with that. That's not an anniversary edition in the end, but a new edition. And I fear that V4 will head in the same direction as V20DA.<br /> <br /> So while I really enjoy stuff like V20, Lore of the Clans etc, I am afraid we are heading down political correctness lane with V4 completely disregarding backstory, metaplot and established cannon in an effort to present a game that's up to the frankly riduculous standards of political correctness of the 21st century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:40:46-07:00","id":610773,"title":"","content":"Oh dear. This rather seems to be turning into &quot;I hate this developer&quot;, &quot;No, that developer is the one who sucks&quot;. While there are things that I dislike about any given game line, I'm a big fan of both Achilli's work on Masquerade and Rose Bailey's root-and-branch re-imagining of Requiem, and I loved David Hill's revival of DA. Vampire. Anyway, none of them are helming this: MMM is the one in the driving seat. There's no need to turn personal taste into personal attacks.<br /> <br /> Getting back on topic: my original questions were why they needed a new edition when we had V20 relatively recently, and would a new edition that was primarily about mechanics revisions appeal to the more setting-orientated cWoD fanbase? If they're taking this on from the 2nd-edition-plus default of V20, and giving us a fully-realized, post-2004 history and game setting along with better mechanics, then that looks like an answer to both my questions. My curiosity is definitely piqued.I'm going to follow this with interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T06:41:02-07:00","id":610774,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to this. Mostly because every time I read the V20 book I have a great feeling of nostalgia, but when I look at the rules I don't see myself playing it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7121-chapolimx","user":"ChapolimX","date":". 08-01-2015, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7121-chapolimx","name":"ChapolimX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T07:01:57-07:00","id":610775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610773#post610773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, none of them are helming this: MMM is the one in the driving seat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is MMM?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610773#post610773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting back on topic: my original questions were why they needed a new edition when we had V20 relatively recently, and would a new edition that was primarily about mechanics revisions appeal to the more setting-orientated cWoD fanbase? If they're taking this on from the 2nd-edition-plus default of V20, and giving us a fully-realized, post-2004 history and game setting along with better mechanics, then that looks like an answer to both my questions. My curiosity is definitely piqued.I'm going to follow this with interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay... Could be interesting... But still I am skeptical...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T07:24:37-07:00","id":610789,"title":"","content":"Matt presumably, which is really cool.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I don't know about you folks but maybe it's a good idea to lay off with the &quot;oh Jebus! It's gonna suck!&quot; and &quot;You're not getting another red cent from me OPP!&quot; until, you know, an ACTUAL announcement is made at least?<br /> And quit with the writer bashing.<br /> It's cheap and lame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T07:31:04-07:00","id":610794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610712#post610712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WHAT? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That makes even less sense. If Gehenna happening in 2004 is cannon, then I don't see how the game line is viable at all. We either have no vampires at all, or we have mostly neonates who know nothing about the decades of backstory (thus,rendering it moot) and end up with a Requiem-like situation...</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly no sects. We are back to a more Dark Ages approach. I also don't think that the only survivors would be neonates, but that a good number of older vampires would survive by basically hiding until it was over. I'm also assuming that Gehenna will push the standard generation down, in the case of having a handful of 4th-8th generation vampires in the world and making most PCs fall into the 14th-9th bracket. I expect to either see something happen to the 14th and 15th generation vampires or for 16th generation vampires to appear. We've had 10+ years to rebuild vampire society and rediscover the backstory, I believe that things such as establishing new sects and finding Beckett's chronicle of Gehenna could be things that you could incorporate into a post-Gehenna chronicle.<br /> <br /> And maybe, just maybe, the Camarilla and/or the Sabbat WON Gehenna. What would happen if the current 'elders' destroyed their forebearers and decided to let Noddism flourish and have all the old backstory be better knowledge? With the Antediluvians undeniably dead and the threat of Gehenna averted, what need do the biggest badest vampires around have to worry about not having always been the pinnacle of power, what matters is that they are now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actuall, no. Not after what you have done with VtR 2.0. The nWoD 2.0 clearly shows that people with a good grip on game design have left the building. I don't see OPP without someone like Justin Achilles in any shape to produce new rules. If you get him on board, I am in. But if mediocre designers like David Hill are allowed to take the helm on this, I am out. My confidence in OPP producing quality rules and quality games are at an all-time low. </div> </div> </div>Umm... VtR 2.0 is an all-round improvement on 1e rules-wise, getting rid of the horrible 'character generation optimisation minigame' where you wanted to spend your free dots optimally in order to not waste XP later was a brilliant idea, because there is now a smaller difference between the 'legless retarded machine-gun operator' and the 'jack of all trades' in the long-run, in that the first now spends as much or more XP to get to being as well-rounded as the jack, who can decide his focus later without the system punishing him for it.<br /> <br /> Beats, Conditions, and Aspirations also give us a key clue as to what the game was designed to do tell a story. By adding to the story you get the ability to make your character stronger, by making your character's goals part of the story you get the ability to make your character stronger. The games-design in VtR 2.0 is brilliant, because the developers decided 1) what sort of game they wanted to make and 2) how to get there. Not all the rules are perfect, but the only changes to the core engine has been the Experience system and adding in Conditions. Pretty much everything has built on what was already there, to make a game that brought fourth the intent of 1e better.<br /> <br /> VtR 2.0 is not a Gamist game, or a Simulationist game, it is a game focused on the Narrative and provides mechanics to support that. Which makes it better designed than any edition of Vampire: the Masquerade or Vampire: the Requiem 1e in my book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T07:55:16-07:00","id":610837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChapolimX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610774#post610774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking forward to this. Mostly because every time I read the V20 book I have a great feeling of nostalgia, but when I look at the rules I don't see me playing it again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I kind of wish they'd just save us all time and scrape Changeling20 and do a new edition rather than a nostalgia book. I'd say the same for Wraith, but it's probably too far along at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T08:21:03-07:00","id":610846,"title":"","content":"Or at least make it a bit more clear what the framework for the 20th supplements are going to be.<br /> <br /> I think, if the 20th books were just core books (since they're compatible enough with most of the older supplements anyway) without a bunch of supplements, people wouldn't react as poorly to the a new edition being in the works as well.<br /> <br /> Since it's way to late to fix that, the best thing to do would be to decide on exactly what supplements the 20th lines really need, and make it clear that those supplements are going to be it to the fans, and it will cut down a bit on the &quot;It's too soon!&quot; reactions. Not get rid of, since you can't, but at least temper them by getting people off the idea that the 20th books were going to see a full suite of supplements more akin to 2e or Rev.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T09:44:16-07:00","id":610937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610738#post610738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pair him with the current VtR 2.0 writers. Rose Bailey and her team are kickass at writing the setting parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, I've written more than anyone else in VtR2.0, by no small margin. I wrote 60,000 words of the book's final 180,000 words. And the book had twelve authors in total. <br /> <br /> But no, I'm not in charge of it. I just consulted a bit. I don't know if or how much I'll be involved. It's Eddy's project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:43:20-07:00","id":611060,"title":"","content":"Will be interesting. I like nwod (2.0 more than 1.0) but have to admit I MISS the old metaplot and the owod demons (although with the translation guide I can bring them to 2.0 nwod). Will be interesting to hear what the devs have in mind there with Gehenna happened. Willl be interesting if any antidevulan has survived and also what will become of the sects if Gehenna has happened and is over already.<br /> <br /> With the other gamelines also existing already (thanks to the CWOD) I sincerly hope taht they will be more compatible to each other in terms of rules. <br /> Also what will be interesting is as Gehenna happened.......if the Apocalypse from Werewolf also happened, ... And more than that almost how hidden it happened. I mean how many big cities were already destroyed in the metaplot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:52:12-07:00","id":611067,"title":"","content":"Post Gehenna? Now I have this image of a Mad Max style world with vampires stuck in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3117-lucius","name":"Lucius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:55:44-07:00","id":611076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611067#post611067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post Gehenna? Now I have this image of a Mad Max style world with vampires stuck in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>yea, wasn't gehenna supposed to be well the apocolpyse? does this mean that vtm 4th is a post-apoc vampire game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:00:18-07:00","id":611080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609620#post609620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I seriously wonder if that's the plan. It seems quite possible.<br /> <br /> At very least, with a new edition not restrained by &quot;nostalgia value&quot; like V20 was, expect them to move away from &quot;multiple actions&quot; as a mechanical thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which i just realized is totally going to screw vampires for crossover purposes until we get new editions of all the lines - DAMN IT!<br /> <br /> With Wraith &amp; Changeling I officially give Onyx Path my blessing to call the lines &quot;4th Edition&quot;, just so everyone is on the same page about which lines go with which - despite the fact that they're technically 3rd Editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:46:43-07:00","id":611117,"title":"","content":"The point is to be Vampire the Masquerade but more modern. VtM is not post-apoc. Even if some sort of Gehenna occurred, we're going to be left with a game of personal horror in Gothic cities. I would assume anything resembling werewolf's apocalypse is not on the plate. If there was Gehenna, it was probably very contained. Personally, I question Gehenna happening at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:02:47-07:00","id":611129,"title":"","content":"If I had to pick up a reason to bash at Onyx Path right now that would be the kind of announcement of an announcement they made. If they were going to make such an announcement at Gen-Con why not let a blog post ready to go. I'm obsessed with monday now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7121-chapolimx","user":"ChapolimX","date":". 08-01-2015, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7121-chapolimx","name":"ChapolimX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:17:26-07:00","id":611149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChapolimX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611129#post611129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had to pick up a reason to bash at Onyx Path right now this would be the kind of announcement of an announcement they made. If they were going to make such an announcement at Gen-Con why not let a blog post ready to go. I'm obsessed with monday now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poor little monday don't stalk it too much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (sry couldn't resist).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is to be Vampire the Masquerade but more modern. VtM is not post-apoc. Even if some sort of Gehenna occurred, we're going to be left with a game of personal horror in Gothic cities. I would assume anything resembling werewolf's apocalypse is not on the plate. If there was Gehenna, it was probably very contained. Personally, I question Gehenna happening at all. </div> </div> </div>That is what I thought. Same could be true for the other gamelines though that it was more hidden than anything else...or parts got &quot;resetted&quot; but lets see there what they say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:41:24-07:00","id":611211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moogle001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611117#post611117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is to be Vampire the Masquerade but more modern. VtM is not post-apoc. Even if some sort of Gehenna occurred, we're going to be left with a game of personal horror in Gothic cities. I would assume anything resembling werewolf's apocalypse is not on the plate. If there was Gehenna, it was probably very contained. Personally, I question Gehenna happening at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't the revised convention books that led up to M20 mention some kind of false start to a catastrophe that never actually happened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:49:37-07:00","id":611231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611149#post611149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poor little monday don't stalk it too much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (sry couldn't resist).<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all right. Luckly someone called me to hang out. Monday can be alone for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7121-chapolimx","name":"ChapolimX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:02:08-07:00","id":611252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611211#post611211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't the revised convention books that led up to M20 mention some kind of false start to a catastrophe that never actually happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence my: <br /> &quot;But I can't help but wonder what this means for the metaplot.<br /> Are we going to see another &quot;the end times haven't happened yet&quot; ala V20?<br /> A Revised Convention book take of &quot;It came. It went. Nothing special happened&quot;.<br /> Or, dare I say it a post-Gehenna setting of &quot;the world went to hell. This is what happened next&quot;?&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: That wasn't a dig Saur. There are an awful lot of posts to read here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":1309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","user":"Andreas Rayne","date":". 08-01-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:13:43-07:00","id":611260,"title":"","content":"Put my vote in as someone who's happy about this. I've enjoyed most of the V20 books thus far released(with the exception of the V20 companion) and I'm eagerly awaiting future V20 books(especially Beckett's Jyhad Diary).<br /> <br /> But I'd also love to see a post-Gehenna take on Vampire, and 4th Edition is something I'd really love to see and play. Onyx Path hasn't let me down yet, and I have no reason to believe they will in the future.<br /> <br /> Wost part about this(and any of OP's products, really : )?<br /> <br /> The wait.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:45:56-07:00","id":611284,"title":"","content":"In V4 I would forget about Gehena altogether and pick it up from the Camarilla Sabat war. Bring back all those characters we use to love and hate and play from there. <br /> <br /> Gehenna is the end in VTM and although I must admit a post-apocaliptic setting is kind of appealling, it would be a whole different game and better served as a supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7120-phelios","name":"Phelios","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T14:04:32-07:00","id":611327,"title":"","content":"I know for me personally, if the announcement had instead been that Wraith 20 and Changing 20 would feature an updated ruleset, and that after they were published an updated VtM would be published officially ringing in a 4e ruleset and meta plot, I would not have been anywhere near as pissed about this announcement.<br /> <br /> Sure, the X20's are &quot;nostalgia books&quot;, but a lot of us fans of cWoD are buying them because we don't like nWoD, and the X20's are the cleanest, most complete versions of cWoD available. <br /> Now, before we even own all the stuff (Lore of the Clans, Wraith 20, etc.), we hear those are no longer going to be the newest versions of those games... While we are still buying the other versions.<br /> It feels ridiculous and unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I also disagree that new players are not interested in the X20 stuff. I've introduced a whole new generation of fans to V20, and have people who can't wait to play M20.<br /> <br /> RPG's are investments that can last a lifetime. I don't have the time to play every rpg I purchase immediately. Many sit on my shelf for years before getting the opportunity or time to play. So I pay a fortune for this ultimate edition of Werewolf 20 on Kickstarter, and now, in all likelihood, before I run it there will be a new edition.<br /> <br /> Not really trying to convince anyone, just my 2 cents about being a fan who feels kicked in the balls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3651,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","user":"Grimmshade","date":". 08-01-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T14:45:28-07:00","id":611383,"title":"","content":"So, from the looks of things, V4 may be continuing the Revised metaplot and possibly even be a post-Gehenna/post-apocalyptic chronicle? Eh, I think I will hold off on this one and stick to V20 for now. That being said, if V4 comes out and it's actually well-written and handles things in a new, refreshing way then I may buy it. So, in other words, I will wait before I jump on board this train that is Vampire: The Masquerade 4th Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:44:09-07:00","id":611420,"title":"","content":"I don't see how a post-Gehenna metaplot can preserve the core premise of the game (it's not named <i>Vampire: the Running from Torchbearing Mobs</i> after all). Unless they have Gehenna be an even less extensive version of the whimper-not-a-bang scenario from the book of the same name so that not only is the general public unaware of vampires, but a wide variety of them survived with their coverup infrastructure still working.<br /> <br /> I'm guardedly optimistic about McElroy developing from a conceptual standpoint, but for the love of God please hire a copy editor/proofreader with actual credentials instead of Mr. Magoo or whoever held that job (if, in fact, anyone did) on <i>Dread Names</i>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T16:15:02-07:00","id":611435,"title":"","content":"How about this: Caine wakes up, kills all vampires of the 9th Generation or lower, goes back to sleep.<br /> <br /> The Generations 8+ were left wondering what happened and found that their blood had thickened. Now they could hold more blood (but the trait limit of 5 remained).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3117-lucius","name":"Lucius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T17:27:13-07:00","id":611489,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#292F33\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Haters gonna hate, bitches gonna bitch, whiners gonna whine, and naysayers gonna naysay, but in the end we'll have Vampire the Masquerade 4 the same and I hope it kicks all kinds of asses. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1119,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","user":"Primal Flame","date":"08-01-2015, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T18:39:54-07:00","id":611586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610712#post610712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WHAT? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That makes even less sense. If Gehenna happening in 2004 is cannon, then I don't see how the game line is viable at all. We either have no vampires at all, or we have mostly neonates who know nothing about the decades of backstory (thus,rendering it moot) and end up with a Requiem-like situation...</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610794#post610794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost certainly no sects. We are back to a more Dark Ages approach. I also don't think that the only survivors would be neonates, but that a good number of older vampires would survive by basically hiding until it was over. I'm also assuming that Gehenna will push the standard generation down, in the case of having a handful of 4th-8th generation vampires in the world and making most PCs fall into the 14th-9th bracket. I expect to either see something happen to the 14th and 15th generation vampires or for 16th generation vampires to appear. We've had 10+ years to rebuild vampire society and rediscover the backstory, I believe that things such as establishing new sects and finding Beckett's chronicle of Gehenna could be things that you could incorporate into a post-Gehenna chronicle.<br /> <br /> And maybe, just maybe, the Camarilla and/or the Sabbat WON Gehenna. What would happen if the current 'elders' destroyed their forebears and decided to let Noddism flourish and have all the old backstory be better knowledge? With the Antediluvians undeniably dead and the threat of Gehenna averted, what need do the biggest, baddest vampires around have to worry about not having always been the pinnacle of power, what matters is that they are now.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611067#post611067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post Gehenna? Now I have this image of a Mad Max style world with vampires stuck in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moogle001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611117#post611117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is to be Vampire the Masquerade but more modern. VtM is not post-apocalypse. Even if some sort of Gehenna occurred, we're going to be left with a game of personal horror in Gothic cities. I would assume anything resembling werewolf's apocalypse is not on the plate. If there was Gehenna, it was probably very contained. Personally, I question Gehenna happening at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phelios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611284#post611284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In V4 I would forget about Gehena altogether and pick it up from the Camarilla-Sabbat war. Bring back all those characters we use to love and hate and play from there.<br /> <br /> Gehenna is the end in VTM and although I must admit a post-apocalyptic setting is kind of appealing, it would be a whole different game and better served as a supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Color me somewhat skeptical of V:tM4. When I first heard of this, the first thing I thought was &quot;Why so soon after V20?&quot; Then I saw the response that 5 years is not all that long between editions, so that mollified me, at least on that front. While I am a fan of metaplot, I do see the appeal of discarding parts of metaplot that don't make sense or that I dislike. But then again, Storytellers have always had that option.<br /> <br /> As for V4th being &quot;post-Gehenna,&quot; I can't see that being viable. The idea of a &quot;quiet Apocalypse&quot; has always struck me as trite and silly. The entire point of an apocalypse is that it's supposed to be the <i>end of the world</i>. That's not the sort of thing that can creep up on you or anyone else (or especially <i>everyone </i>else) without the world, y'know, <i>noticing</i>.<br /> It's not like people wake up one morning, go to work and remark around the water cooler with stuff like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Hey, did you know the world ended last week?&quot;<br /> &quot;You don't say? I didn't notice a thing.&quot;<br /> &quot;Wait, what? The world ended? Why am I always the last to hear about this sort of thing? They didn't shit about this on CNN!&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, they <b><i>did </i></b>mention it on Fox News, but then Fox is <b><i>always </i></b>predicting the imminent end of civilization, so I didn't pay attention...&quot;<br /> &quot;Huh. The world ended. Go figure. So what are you guys doing this weekend?&quot; </div> </div> </div>No. I'm hardly an expert in eschatology (despite being a big fan of Werewolf: the Apocalypse), but I'm quite certain that apocalypses don't work like that. Even taking the &quot;Wormwood&quot; scenario from ToJ: Gehenna into account (an example of a &quot;quiet apocalypse&quot; if ever there was one), there's no way V:tM would be even be the same game if the metaplot tried to be &quot;post-Gehenna.&quot; No matter how you slice it, whether it's a &quot;quiet&quot; one or not, an apocalypse <i>by its very definition</i> is the total up-ending of the status quo. If OPP is bringing the metaplot back for V4th, the only way it will make any sense is if Gehenna is still on the horizon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 08-01-2015, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:10:14-07:00","id":611636,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty certain this has turned me off X20, which saves me a lot of money. There's a new edition of Unknown Armies on the horizon. That game hasn't been updated for 13 years, so it seems a more solid investment. <br /> Good luck and have fun all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:18:21-07:00","id":611656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611636#post611636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty certain this has turned me off X20, which saves me a lot of money. There's a new edition of Unknown Armies on the horizon. That game hasn't been updated for 13 years, so it seems a more solid investment.<br /> Good luck and have fun all!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's gonna be at least a year before V4th is out when we can judge it on its own merits and he's leaving now? I admit I'm skeptical of V4th but I'm going to give it a chance to impress me despite my initial (and admittedly somewhat irrational) misgivings. In any case, we have at least a year before anyone has any right to talk any smack about this new edition.<br /> <br /> I predict Grimmshade will be back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:42:48-07:00","id":611675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610773#post610773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, none of them are helming this: MMM is the one in the driving seat.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he isn't.<br /> <br /> Current VTM developer Eddy Webb is going to continue to be the Vampire developer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T19:56:26-07:00","id":611706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeebers76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=610724#post610724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ich. I can't stand Justin Achilles' terrible writing skills! He was an okay developer but he couldn't write for (bleep)! New York by Night and the two Giovanni clanbooks plus the Giovanni clan novel was his baby, and all sucked rocks.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Don't make personal attacks.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:04:16-07:00","id":611711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611636#post611636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty certain this has turned me off X20, which saves me a lot of money. There's a new edition of Unknown Armies on the horizon. That game hasn't been updated for 13 years, so it seems a more solid investment. <br /> Good luck and have fun all!</div> </div> </div> </div>I need a source on that new edition of Unknown Armies ASAP.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I fucking love that game. It's everything Mage wishes it could be and I've been craving a new edition for years now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T20:13:47-07:00","id":611723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611711#post611711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I need a source on that new edition of Unknown Armies ASAP.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I fucking love that game. It's everything Mage wishes it could be and I've been craving a new edition for years now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard of Unknown Armies until Grimmshade mentioned it, but according to their website, there's no new news since January. If the official website doesn't have any news on a new edition, how did Grimmshade hear of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T21:01:08-07:00","id":611833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611489#post611489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#292F33\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Haters gonna hate, bitches gonna bitch, whiners gonna whine, and naysayers gonna naysay, but in the end we'll have Vampire the Masquerade 4 the same and I hope it kicks all kinds of asses. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Couldn't have said it any better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T21:06:18-07:00","id":611835,"title":"","content":"If it really is post-Gehenna, and a &quot;soft Gehenna&quot; at that, I'm out. The entire rationale given for having Gehenna happen was to deliver on the much-promised Big Ending. To find out this Big Ending isn't that big after all is a massive let-down.<br /> <br /> Likewise if the ruleset is massively different from what came before, I'm out. I play cWoD because I know the mechanics. Between each iteration of the game, the tweaks were small enough that I didn't have to learn an entirely new game to keep playing my old one. If I have to do that, why would I learn a brand new VtM when I can just (finally) spend the time to learn VtR? I don't have enough time to start memorizing an entire new ruleset just to play a game I've been playing for two decades.<br /> <br /> But until something official about this new edition has been released, I'll remain skeptically optimistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T21:18:50-07:00","id":611841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611835#post611835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise if the ruleset is massively different from what came before, I'm out. I play cWoD because I know the mechanics. Between each iteration of the game, the tweaks were small enough that I didn't have to learn an entirely new game to keep playing my old one. If I have to do that, why would I learn a brand new VtM when I can just (finally) spend the time to learn VtR? I don't have enough time to start memorizing an entire new ruleset just to play a game I've been playing for two decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm certain that is exactly what Onyx would like people to do: if you're happy with what you have, keep on going. As they say, your books aren't bursting into flames (which, incidentally, is more or less what happens with a lot of video games these days). However, I still think you'll find plenty of difference between the themes and styles of VtR vs VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T21:19:08-07:00","id":611842,"title":"","content":"You know...in first ed gehenna wasn't a myth. It was known fact.<br /> <br /> And it was every few millenia the antideluvians rise eat a whole bunch of really old vampires becuase they are hungry and then go back to sleep.<br /> <br /> Kinda was just a purge of ancient blooded vampires. <br /> <br /> That was way back in first ed though. <br /> <br /> Random fact of the day if you can get your hands on a copy of vampire the masquerade first edition hehe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T21:25:57-07:00","id":611865,"title":"","content":"Atamajakki and Su-teph, I PM'd you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3651-grimmshade","name":"Grimmshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T21:40:41-07:00","id":611872,"title":"","content":"And speaking of updated metaplot, has anybody looked at the metaplot laid out in VTM: MET 20th anniversary edition? It tells of the events that took place after '04, and more than likely what going to be what's presented in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. And if it isn't, then It could be what we see in 4th.ED.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T23:58:21-07:00","id":611943,"title":"","content":"Very unhappy with this and heres the 2 main reasons why: first, if i understand correctly, V4 will be a departure from the foundation of cWoD - 'its our world but with hidden supernatural forces' - and will be instead a much more alternate world. Following on from that, V20 (and thus the original setting) will no longer be supported.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T00:40:58-07:00","id":611954,"title":"","content":"Vampire was my introduction to WoD, and my introduction to RPGs other than DnD. I have a real soft spot for it, so I want to be excited about this. Part of me just is, because it's Vampire.<br /> <br /> But, I've spent large amounts of 21st century money building my collection of WoD. That's hard-earned, adult money, rather than easy-come, easy-go kid money. A part of me is irked that V20 isn't even finished, I have yet to see a new Wraith (a game I have always wanted to own and play) and now I hear that a few developers are dividing their attention further on yet another line.<br /> <br /> I'm going to withhold judgment, and allow OPP time to present their marketing proposition here, but their hype machine doesn't work on me anymore. I want some solid answers on why I should buy this product. I have no use for 21st century political correctness. I have no use for yet another slightly different take on some random Clan, or a minor update to a rule set I long ago banged into usability myself (I'm looking at you, Vicissitude).<br /> <br /> What is definitively new, exciting, AND better about this edition?<br /> <br /> Also, I gotta say that this smacks of last-minutism. Why announce a 4th Edition of a much-loved game without any marketing materials ready to go? Is it because they were going to GenCon without the other huge product they have been delaying for years, again, and they needed something big to get attention? Well, it worked, OPP, you have my attention.<br /> <br /> Now sell me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T01:54:32-07:00","id":611968,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m a bit ambiguous about this as a project. The 20th Anniversary Edition was kinda sold as being a \u2018definitive\u2019 edition (with Requiem as a more \u2018modern' alternative), but time moves on I guess in all things. If there is a new edition, I guess some things could be looked at: <br /> <br /> a) Bring back the iconic red rose on the cover. Why did it have to go in the first place? <br /> b) Get better art for the Clan splat pages. Nothing personal to Leif Jones, as some of his work is really good, but\u2019s it\u2019s never been the right style and wasn\u2019t anything like as evocative as the drawings used in the 2nd edition. <br /> c) Take the game back to basics a bit. Remove the bloat, streamline the rules and tighten the themes. As with point b), I always prefered the 2nd edition of the game with the seven Camarilla Clans, and the general lean-ness of the book generally. It was more accessible to play, and I\u2019d imagine would cost less in postage and packaging. <br /> d) Look at the cultural trends of the 21st century and integrate the setting more to the world and events we see around us. My view is that original Vampire was actually something of a satire of the 80s in fact (despite being released in the early 90s). That was thirty years ago. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, I\u2019ll reserve judgement on the game till it comes out. This may be a while away in any case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T06:03:20-07:00","id":612111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611968#post611968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m a bit ambiguous about this as a project. The 20th Anniversary Edition was kinda sold as being a \u2018definitive\u2019 edition (with Requiem as a more \u2018modern' alternative), but time moves on I guess in all things. If there is a new edition, I guess some things could be looked at:<br /> <br /> a) Bring back the iconic red rose on the cover. Why did it have to go in the first place?<br /> b) Get better art for the Clan splat pages. Nothing personal to Leif Jones, as some of his work is really good, but\u2019s it\u2019s never been the right style and wasn\u2019t anything like as evocative as the drawings used in the 2nd edition.<br /> c) Take the game back to basics a bit. Remove the bloat, streamline the rules and tighten the themes. As with point b), I always prefered the 2nd edition of the game with the seven Camarilla Clans, and the general lean-ness of the book generally. It was more accessible to play, and I\u2019d imagine would cost less in postage and packaging.<br /> d) Look at the cultural trends of the 21st century and integrate the setting more to the world and events we see around us. My view is that original Vampire was actually something of a satire of the 80s in fact (despite being released in the early 90s). That was thirty years ago.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I\u2019ll reserve judgement on the game till it comes out. This may be a while away in any case.</div> </div> </div> </div>For b) I agree that the 2e art on the clan spreads was awesome (baring the Malkavian and Toreador for me in the corebook, that that's because they feel 'boring' to me, still evocative of the clans), although I do love the V20 versions, especially the Malkavian.<br /> <br /> If this is going to happen I think that the developers have to decide how the Clans look in a post-Gehenna world. Are they rarer, with the majority of Cainites being Caitiff? Have they changed, with their roles being vastly different? (oh how I would like to see the Tremere as the hunted ones for a change) Are they the same, just with different ones as the prominent ones?<br /> <br /> I hope that they run V20 and VtM4e side by side, with V20 offering sourcebooks for the classic setting and mechanics, and 4e giving use cleaned up mechanics and a setting where the young vampires have inherited vampire society after the latest Gehenna. Now they have to prepare for when the ancients rise again in several thousand years and squabble amongst themselves.<br /> <br /> But I definitely want cleaned-up rules and defined guidelines for building inceptor disciplines. I actually like the idea that Gehenna has happened, the vampire world was destroyed and rebuilt 10 years ago, but the younger inheritors have rebuilt the tyranny of their elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:18:10-07:00","id":612316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611943#post611943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very unhappy with this and heres the 2 main reasons why: first, if i understand correctly, V4 will be a departure from the foundation of cWoD - 'its our world but with hidden supernatural forces' - and will be instead a much more alternate world. Following on from that, V20 (and thus the original setting) will no longer be supported.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it will almost assuredly not be a departure of setting. Not alternate world, the Classic World of Darkness, but more modern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Fallen CoD/X20 Revamp</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-arch-spheres\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension Arch-Spheres</a><br /> <a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/mage-the-ascension-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">Mage: The Ascension CoD/X20 Revamp</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6807-moogle001","name":"moogle001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:22:17-07:00","id":612318,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'd just prefer to have fewer bloodlines (they got out of control to say the least) and fewer Independent clans (again, most are marked &quot;does not play well with others&quot;). I can do that with V20 already. Why would I need a new edition in the first place? I have all that I need. The only thing I didn't like about V20 was how they did hunting and the 3 physical Disciplines. Fixed that pretty quick already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6752-jeebers76","name":"Jeebers76","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:47:24-07:00","id":612337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moogle001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=612316#post612316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, it will almost assuredly not be a departure of setting. Not alternate world, the Classic World of Darkness, but more modern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not officially. But. Last time I looked, the world did not nearly end about a decade ago. So either its a different and alternate history, or Gehenna had no teeth, and both those options deviate from and weaken the original premise.<br /> Regardless, it looks like the V20 line is coming to an end, pretty soon, and thats a shock and feels like a letdown to a lot of us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 08-02-2015, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T10:31:43-07:00","id":612398,"title":"","content":"There is one other possibility : Gehenna is slow. I mean, most of the real elder introduced to the game have century of torpor to shake off, Hakim send Ur-Shulgi maybe because he have a very hard case of &quot;morning after&quot;. Ten years for us is just a blink of en eye for someone who lived ten thousand of years ! So, maybe the Anarch unbounds, the Kuei-Jin invasion, the Sabbat Fourth civil war looming, etc is just the start of everything.<br /> Or something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T10:44:49-07:00","id":612404,"title":"","content":"I only wonder if it's the start of a reboot for everything, or if it's just gonna be Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T11:18:09-07:00","id":612431,"title":"","content":"I think it'll be like the MRev Convention Books, where the End Times was just a false start. Gehenna might still be coming, but not yet...<br /> <br /> What was in the V20 MET book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T11:51:27-07:00","id":612471,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I don\u2019t think this is going to be like a DnD-style Third-&gt;Fourth-&gt;Fifth transition. Looking back, there are fair differences between First Edition and Revised but nothing players can\u2019t make [easily?] compatible with V20. Heck, I still remember using some First Edition material for Revised games. Did it require some tweaking? Yes. How much? Like fifteen minutes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Anecdote: Going from First and Second Edition, I remember thinking how cool it was dividing the fluff and crunch with \u201cSystem:\u201d in the Disciplines chapter. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> *throws two oboli on table</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T13:15:05-07:00","id":612532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=609811#post609811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, something about trying to get the old setting up and running again seems...incorrect. The cWoD was all about the impending apocalypses, and since we actually got those it seems weird to keep moving forward with it (Not that the apocalypses we got we all that great). Plus, the entire point of the old system ending was because the well had run dry, and the metaplot had stretched things to their limit. Not to mention after ten or so years a lot of the flaws in the setting had become too huge to ignore and too ingrained to alter.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>the whole gehenna/apocalyspe/whatever happening with all the stuff heralding it in is what leaves me rather puzzled...&quot;gehenna? nah, it was just a false start&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","name":"Nigredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:09:54-07:00","id":612588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperSabbatST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=611842#post611842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know...in first ed gehenna wasn't a myth. It was known fact.<br /> <br /> And it was every few millenia the antideluvians rise eat a whole bunch of really old vampires becuase they are hungry and then go back to sleep.<br /> <br /> Kinda was just a purge of ancient blooded vampires.<br /> <br /> That was way back in first ed though.<br /> <br /> Random fact of the day if you can get your hands on a copy of vampire the masquerade first edition hehe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the idea of what Gehenna is seems to have changed from a cyclical event to the End of Times going to Rev (possibly already when they added WtA to the fold), though. I prefer the idea of the cyclic event, but that's kind of different than what they have presented in the last edition, and recanting would need quite a bit of work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","user":"Nigredo","date":". 08-02-2015, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","name":"Nigredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:45:26-07:00","id":612614,"title":"","content":"I WANT something like the transition between D&amp;D 3.5 and 5th. Staying so close to the old editions means you can't change any of the real problems. You can only tweak. VtM NEED some major updates that won't be backwards compatible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:56:08-07:00","id":612626,"title":"","content":"What if they make it using the Sardonyx system? Both similar and different enough to the WoD (classic and new)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T15:32:32-07:00","id":612681,"title":"","content":"I'm only interested because I'm looking forward to a bold revision of the rules. The metaplot is not a problem to me since I can easily use or ignore whatever I want. If VTM 4e turns out into something I don't like I might try to use V20 with VTR 2e rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7121-chapolimx","name":"ChapolimX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T15:52:13-07:00","id":612756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=612626#post612626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if they make it using the Sardonyx system? Both similar and different enough to the WoD (classic and new)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would be happy with that. I like what we've seen so far, and being able to have vampires with my Scion would make me happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T17:48:56-07:00","id":612852,"title":"","content":"- The Withering happened<br /> - Theo Bell killed Hardestdat, and van Pieterzoon took over the Camarilla<br /> - The Week of Nightmares happened. There are no more Ravno, though I guess you could say that maybe a handful survived, so Ravnos players won't be too upset.(my best friend was a Ravnos, and when WW killed them off he was like &quot;wtf?&quot;)<br /> - The Gangrel are reconsidering joining the Camarilla.<br /> - Moncada has been killed by Lucita, who became the new archbishop of Madrid. She could possibly take over the entire Sabbat, though of course Vykos won't accept it easily.<br /> - The Tremere have also nearly been completely wiped out. Not a single member of the Tremere inner circle survived. Tremere neonates have a chance at freedom for the first time.<br /> - Beckett is still doing his thing, digging up ancient lore etc<br /> - Augustus Giovanni is dead. The Giovanni have splintered into several smaller clans.<br /> - Fatima killed Ur Shulgi using Haqim's sword and became the first old woman of the mountain<br /> - Lasombra brought in a week long night, mankind almost found out about the supernatural, but rather a scientific explanation was offered<br /> - Anatole is dead and gone, though he could appear to his old friends in dreams, hallucinations, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T18:57:28-07:00","id":612893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=612404#post612404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only wonder if it's the start of a reboot for everything, or if it's just gonna be Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the big 3 will get a 4th if V4 sells well enough. Maybe the other lines,depending on sales and reception","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:10:51-07:00","id":612897,"title":"","content":"I wonder how they'll do a WtA4th. Considering the 'Apocalypse' was kind of a BIG part of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:31:12-07:00","id":612903,"title":"","content":"I remember the cyclic thing, and had forgotten about it until now.<br /> I started with 2nd Edition so surely it was in there somewhere.<br /> Or am I a victim of retrograde lore?<br /> <br /> Edit: Now I've got to unpack my second ed books and start scouring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:34:04-07:00","id":612906,"title":"","content":"The 2nd edition Core was very close to the 1st edition one, and I think the bit of the Kindred 'historian' (I think he was) who recounted Gehennas was in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:39:41-07:00","id":612911,"title":"","content":"My god!<br /> Now that would be cool as hell.<br /> Something that was listed in previous editions as a cycle, that was forgotten in later editions (and by the fans) suddenly reared its head again.<br /> That's...that's amazing.<br /> I'm probably completely wrong but that simple idea blows my mind.<br /> <br /> Edit: If this is actually what happens I will name my first born in honour of the person who thought it out.<br /> Eddy Dodd is pretty cool right? Or Ian? Or Matt? Or Rich even?<br /> Justin? I offered Justin cookies and he wouldn't eat them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":1309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","user":"Andreas Rayne","date":". 08-02-2015, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:07:04-07:00","id":612933,"title":"","content":"For those wondering this is the text in question;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mortal history records a time, beginning over two thousand years ago, of burgeoning empires locked in combat with one another - the time of the Persians, the Greeks and the Tartars. Thus did the Fifth Generation establish its own order. Meanwhile, the Antediluvians lay hidden and pursued their own mad schemes. This age of wars may even have been of their making, the beginning of their great Jyhad. Whatever the truth, almost none remain to speak of it. I myself have met only one of the Fifth Generation, and at the time I did not know it.<br /> <br /> It is said by some that near the end of this period, the Antediluvians emerged from their hiding places and sucked the blood of all my kind, each leaving but one new Progeny of their line. This legend has it that this was the close of the Second Cycle, that the Antediluvians' lust for blood was so great that they needed all of my race as their Vessels. Those who believe in the Cycle legends predict an Armageddon in the near future.<br /> <br /> They say that the Antediluvians are asleep now, but someday they will awaken and then they will feed. The Third Cycle is coming to a close, and none but the Third Generation will remain alive at its conclusion. The true believers say that each Cycle lasts 2300 years, and soon, very soon, the time approaches. They call it Gehenna, and some prepare for it fervently. As a man of science, these beliefs seem extreme to me, but they cannot be entirely discounted. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 08-02-2015, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:08:50-07:00","id":612935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=612431#post612431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it'll be like the MRev Convention Books, where the End Times was just a false start. Gehenna might still be coming, but not yet...<br /> <br /> What was in the V20 MET book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The BNS MET isn't V20. It's just MET:VtM, separate from OPPs lines.<br /> <br /> Some of the big metaplot advancements were...<br /> * Gehenna started then stalled to a stop.<br /> * Week of Nightmares happened.<br /> * Cam couldn't deny Antes anymore so they now have a party line of 'Antes are benevolent mothers and fathers!'<br /> * Sabbat suffered heavy losses due to Cam and hunters; they have lost lots of territory and are on the 'hide, investigate, and recover' aspect, rather than RAR BLOODY MONSTERS IN THE STREETS.<br /> * The Giovanni broke The Promise and created the Independent Alliance with the Followers of Set.<br /> * The Gangrel have returned to the Camarilla but hasn't been granted full Pillar Clan status.<br /> * The Assamites are recognized as a Pillar Clan.<br /> <br /> Myself, I REALLY hope that V4 is just not that metaplot turned into a TT book. It'll really feel more like a CCP-mandated thing than anything else at that point, since lots of WoD fans in the LARP community really like the meta changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","user":"thebiglarpnerd","date":". 08-02-2015, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:16:34-07:00","id":612940,"title":"","content":"Small clarification there - the Assamites did not found the Josians, nor is it a development of BNS. Josians first (IIRC) appeared in Archons and Templars back in 2002.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:21:27-07:00","id":612944,"title":"","content":"Whoops. my bad. I've edited such. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:22:04-07:00","id":612945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BR_Malk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=612852#post612852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Edit: Just conjection/fan theory, and not supported in any books.</b><br /> - The Withering happened<br /> - Theo Bell killed Hardestdat, and van Pieterzoon took over the Camarilla<br /> - The Week of Nightmares happened. There are no more Ravno, though I guess you could say that maybe a handful survived, so Ravnos players won't be too upset.(my best friend was a Ravnos, and when WW killed them off he was like &quot;wtf?&quot;)<br /> - The Gangrel are reconsidering joining the Camarilla.<br /> - Moncada has been killed by Lucita, who became the new archbishop of Madrid. She could possibly take over the entire Sabbat, though of course Vykos won't accept it easily.<br /> - The Tremere have also nearly been completely wiped out. Not a single member of the Tremere inner circle survived. Tremere neonates have a chance at freedom for the first time.<br /> - Beckett is still doing his thing, digging up ancient lore etc<br /> - Augustus Giovanni is dead. The Giovanni have splintered into several smaller clans.<br /> - Fatima killed Ur Shulgi using Haqim's sword and became the first old woman of the mountain<br /> - Lasombra brought in a week long night, mankind almost found out about the supernatural, but rather a scientific explanation was offered<br /> - Anatole is dead and gone, though he could appear to his old friends in dreams, hallucinations, etc</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The BNS MET isn't V20. It's just MET:VtM, separate from OPPs lines.<br /> <br /> The big metaplot advancements were...<br /> * Gehenna started then stalled to a stop.<br /> * Week of Nightmares happened.<br /> * Cam couldn't deny Antes anymore so they now have a party line of 'Antes are benevolent mothers and fathers!'<br /> * Sabbat suffered heavy losses due to Cam and hunters; they have lost lots of territory and are on the 'hide, investigate, and recover' aspect, rather than RAR BLOODY MONSTERS IN THE STREETS.<br /> * The Giovanni broke The Promise and created the Independent Alliance with the Followers of Set.<br /> * The Gangrel have returned to the Camarilla but hasn't been granted full Pillar Clan status.<br /> * The Assamites are recognized as a Pillar Clan, with their own Justicar (Tegyrius) and founded the Josians <b>(this bit is incorrect)</b>, the anti-infernalist Archons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect. I hope this is an indication of what we can expect? It certainly all sounds good to me :P<br /> <br /> With the cyclical Gehennas thing above, it's all starting to make sense. Maybe Beckett's Diary will give us some clues?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Edit: BR_Malk's contribution was just their own theory/preference, rather than anything found in BNS MET. 08-06-2015, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:26:26-07:00","id":612949,"title":"","content":"Thanks for posting these. They give a really nice insight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For those wondering this is the text in question;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Mortal history records a time, beginning over two thousand years ago, of burgeoning empires locked in combat with one another - the time of the Persians, the Greeks and the Tartars. Thus did the Fifth Generation establish its own order. Meanwhile, the Antediluvians lay hidden and pursued their own mad schemes. This age of wars may even have been of their making, the beginning of their great Jyhad. Whatever the truth, almost none remain to speak of it. I myself have met only one of the Fifth Generation, and at the time I did not know it.<br /> <br /> It is said by some that near the end of this period, the Antediluvians emerged from their hiding places and sucked the blood of all my kind, each leaving but one new Progeny of their line. This legend has it that this was the close of the Second Cycle, that the Antediluvians' lust for blood was so great that they needed all of my race as their Vessels. Those who believe in the Cycle legends predict an Armageddon in the near future.<br /> <br /> They say that the Antediluvians are asleep now, but someday they will awaken and then they will feed. The Third Cycle is coming to a close, and none but the Third Generation will remain alive at its conclusion. The true believers say that each Cycle lasts 2300 years, and soon, very soon, the time approaches. They call it Gehenna, and some prepare for it fervently. As a man of science, these beliefs seem extreme to me, but they cannot be entirely discounted.</span></i></span><br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some of the big metaplot advancements were...<br /> * Gehenna started then stalled to a stop.<br /> * Week of Nightmares happened.<br /> * Cam couldn't deny Antes anymore so they now have a party line of 'Antes are benevolent mothers and fathers!'<br /> * Sabbat suffered heavy losses due to Cam and hunters; they have lost lots of territory and are on the 'hide, investigate, and recover' aspect, rather than RAR BLOODY MONSTERS IN THE STREETS.<br /> * The Giovanni broke The Promise and created the Independent Alliance with the Followers of Set.<br /> * The Gangrel have returned to the Camarilla but hasn't been granted full Pillar Clan status.<br /> * The Assamites are recognized as a Pillar Clan, with their own Justicar (Tegyrius) and founded the Josians, the anti-infernalist Archons. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7121-chapolimx","name":"ChapolimX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:30:53-07:00","id":612956,"title":"","content":"What's the source for this information??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:31:43-07:00","id":612957,"title":"","content":"Dreamingod: thank you!<br /> I KNEW I read it somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:32:00-07:00","id":612958,"title":"","content":"Well the blurb I transcribed was from the 2nd Edition WoD core, in the beginning of the first chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T20:37:00-07:00","id":612962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChapolimX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=612949#post612949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for posting these. They give a really nice insight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I don't know where BRMalk's stuff comes from though; there's no mention of Fatima, or Hardestadt's death or really anything he mentioned in MET:VtM (and to double check myself, I went back through and CTRL+F'd my PDF copy, as I was like 'whut?').<br /> <br /> Maybe those are just his ideas for plot for V4.<br /> <br /> Additionally...<br /> <br /> * Theo Bell is the Brujah Justicar<br /> * A new Malkavian, Dona Manuela Bolivar, La Llorona is the new Justicar, and the Sabbat are terrified of the 'Weeping Woman' as they call her.<br /> * The Camarilla have taken many traditionally Sabbat areas in Mexico and South America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5704,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","user":"thebiglarpnerd","date":". 08-02-2015, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T21:09:12-07:00","id":613000,"title":"","content":"Half-serious change for KotE: Tou Mu was never a Yama Queen or anything of the sort. It was all just someone's chili-induced fever dream after reading <i>Deities &amp; Demigods</i> for AD&amp;D. The actual Tou Mu, or Doumu if you will, is hard to disentangle from the layers of prime goddesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T21:57:46-07:00","id":613019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=612897#post612897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how they'll do a WtA4th. Considering the 'Apocalypse' was kind of a BIG part of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>One theory is that that kinfolk still survived. Now that the Wyrm is back in balance the Garou would be given over to it as it's warriors of destruction and death on Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T21:58:50-07:00","id":613020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For those wondering this is the text in question;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Mortal history records a time, beginning over two thousand years ago, of burgeoning empires locked in combat with one another - the time of the Persians, the Greeks and the Tartars. Thus did the Fifth Generation establish its own order. Meanwhile, the Antediluvians lay hidden and pursued their own mad schemes. This age of wars may even have been of their making, the beginning of their great Jyhad. Whatever the truth, almost none remain to speak of it. I myself have met only one of the Fifth Generation, and at the time I did not know it.<br /> <br /> It is said by some that near the end of this period, the Antediluvians emerged from their hiding places and sucked the blood of all my kind, each leaving but one new Progeny of their line. This legend has it that this was the close of the Second Cycle, that the Antediluvians' lust for blood was so great that they needed all of my race as their Vessels. Those who believe in the Cycle legends predict an Armageddon in the near future.<br /> <br /> They say that the Antediluvians are asleep now, but someday they will awaken and then they will feed. The Third Cycle is coming to a close, and none but the Third Generation will remain alive at its conclusion. The true believers say that each Cycle lasts 2300 years, and soon, very soon, the time approaches. They call it Gehenna, and some prepare for it fervently. As a man of science, these beliefs seem extreme to me, but they cannot be entirely discounted</span></i></span>. </div> </div> </div>Good lord, I still have my hardcover copy of V:tM 2nd Ed and I totally forgot that I had read this. (Then again, it <i>was </i>more than 20 years ago.) When it was first mentioned on this thread that Gehenna was a cyclical event, I thought the poster saying that was crazy. But here it is. Yeah, this was never mentioned again in any of the subsequent books.<br /> <br /> That still doesn't diminish my uneasiness at the possibility of V4th having a &quot;soft&quot; Gehenna added to the updated metaplot, but there's nothing for it but to wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T22:14:17-07:00","id":613030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowlost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=613019#post613019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One theory is that that kinfolk still survived. Now that the Wyrm is back in balance the Garou would be given over to it as it's warriors of destruction and death on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would go over like a transuranic lead balloon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T02:26:21-07:00","id":613110,"title":"","content":"I see that a lot of the early posts in this thread are looking forward to a major revision of the rules but seeing that Onyx Path JUST kickstarted V20 Lore of the Clans I can understand the frustration. M20 is a lot more forward thinking concerning metaplot and evolved many of the organizations within its part of cWoD and I can see that V20 could use a similar update. W20 and M20 aren't really simply &quot;nostalgia products&quot;, they are updates to their lines. It would of course be fun to see the same for Vampire.<br /> <br /> I however think that that backwards compatibility with V20 is paramount. Sure, rule updates and a continuation of the metaplot is one thing (I strongly agree with the critique of &quot;Soft Gehenna&quot; but whatever), but VtM4 probably couldn't contradict or make obsolete new or coming books like Lore of the Clans, Rites of Blood or V20 Ghouls. That would be crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5402-malcolmlittle","user":"MalcolmLittle","date":". 08-03-2015, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5402-malcolmlittle","name":"MalcolmLittle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T02:40:46-07:00","id":613114,"title":"","content":"I get that Gencon is extremely tiring for all the people att Onyx Path but to announce a new version of Masquerade and not have some kind of PR push afterward, with follow up info, is not good. I mean, you announce it officially to the greater world via a tweet? Only second hand information from a panel? We all remember Mage Revised; of course the cWoD Community would be divided between anticipation and fearful hesitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5402-malcolmlittle","name":"MalcolmLittle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T09:08:33-07:00","id":613457,"title":"","content":"I too am somewhat flabbergasted at the &quot;stop bothering us about the big announcement we just made, we're too busy to answer any questions about it!&quot; PR strategy. Really, no one at OPP foresaw that the customer base would have lots of questions in the immediate wake of a major controversial announcement at the premiere US gaming event, and made any preparations for the contingency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T09:37:37-07:00","id":613505,"title":"","content":"They gave us a little. They are barely even home! I believe it was said that they would do a blog post about it when everyone was home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:39:01-07:00","id":613641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=613457#post613457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too am somewhat flabbergasted at the &quot;stop bothering us about the big announcement we just made, we're too busy to answer any questions about it!&quot; PR strategy. Really, no one at OPP foresaw that the customer base would have lots of questions in the immediate wake of a major controversial announcement at the premiere US gaming event, and made any preparations for the contingency?</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire staff was at GenCon. That's, like, a pretty huge deal for any RPG company. Today is Monday, when they generally conduct their OP meeting. I would assume there will be answers tonight. It's not that &quot;no one at OPP foresaw&quot; that we'd have questions, it's simply that there was no time to answer them. The book is months away. Months. Relax. Info will be forthcoming.<br /> <br /> Even now, information from some of the OP panels at the show are being leaked out. Slowly but surely. These guys were working 12 hour days. Give them a break, allow them to gain their bearings, and the news will come.<br /> <br /> This is not E3 announcing Fallout 4, with a 15 person public relations team being paid 70k a year with nothing else to do BUT hand out information coinciding with the show.<br /> <br /> This is, like, a four person-staffed pen and paper RPG company.<br /> <br /> Go look up Bruins news. They're in for a rough season this year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:55:44-07:00","id":613658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=613641#post613641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire staff was at GenCon. That's, like, a pretty huge deal for any RPG company. Today is Monday, when they generally conduct their OP meeting. I would assume there will be answers tonight. It's not that &quot;no one at OPP foresaw&quot; that we'd have questions, it's simply that there was no time to answer them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely they had time. They had from the moment the ink dried on the memo saying it's gonna be announced at Gen Con until the moment they walked out of the offices. It's not hard to prepare an announcement blog post ahead of time. Hell, most gaming companies do that when they know a significant number of their fans are gonna want more information that a picture posted to Instagram and shared on Twitter. Even a blog post containing things like: &quot;New post-Gehenna setting! New mechanics! Old clans die, new clans rise!&quot; on their own website would have worked. Instead, the information we have gotten is a tweet made in response to the complaints about a lack of info and a forum-user posting notes. And all on the forums, not even a hint on the main page.<br /> <br /> I mean, they clearly set up some blog posts for later release on the main page, because we're getting updates on what they were playtesting on each day, released on said day. It's not like they don't have the capability to do what they are already doing.<br /> <br /> So I can't imagine why they wouldn't have done the same thing with a major, major announcement like this (they might be a four person-staffed company like you said, but for a company that size this is pretty gawdamn big). Unless the 4th edition was a last minute idea, but I doubt that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T11:29:42-07:00","id":613712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=613658#post613658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the 4th edition was a last minute idea, but I doubt that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I think. The whole thing is so ill prepared that is must have been last minute. Otherwise they could have teased it ahead of time, prepared more than some paper that Eddy holds up on the picture etc. They could have gone in with a prepared presentation, handouts, a timed blog post etc. The way it is currently handled either screams &quot;last minute decision&quot; or &quot;unprofessional work&quot;. Would rather OPP make a last minute decision or be unprofessional? I for one believe they are professional. Which leaves last minute decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T12:00:37-07:00","id":613756,"title":"","content":"Remember...they can't do anything without ccps ok.<br /> <br /> So most likely they pitched it and didn't get the thumbs up till very recently.<br /> <br /> But I'm sure all will be explained soon :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T12:01:06-07:00","id":613757,"title":"","content":"One could argue that if nothing is coming before at least 2017 and it was just a last minute idea, they could have post-poned the announcement until next year and have something to show for it. Understanding the excitement and that they might have wanted to share the fact with the fans and supporters ASAP, it's a tidal wave that was sure to meet with several truckloads of questions and strong reactions - negative or positive - that are a consequence of the lack of more info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","user":"Nigredo","date":". 08-03-2015, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","name":"Nigredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:40:19-07:00","id":613962,"title":"","content":"Well remember dark ages vampire also had gehenna as part of their setting. Many vampires in the dark ages also believed gehenna was coming around the corner with these thin blood 13 gens popping up.<br /> <br /> So I don't think the theme of the end times are coming are gonna go away completely.<br /> <br /> My theory anyways.<br /> <br /> Just hope they don't go with the bns metaplot update. <br /> <br /> I wasn't a fan of that personally. <br /> <br /> I also like the idea of mechanics books and plot books being to seperate things. The problem is usually when you tie your mechanics to the metaplot. Then I as an st have to do work to try to remove that if I don't want to use your metaplot.<br /> <br /> Guess we will have to wait and see!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:54:53-07:00","id":613982,"title":"","content":"except, the Gehenna of revised was more than just paranoia by canon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","user":"Nigredo","date":". 08-03-2015, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","name":"Nigredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T14:00:42-07:00","id":613988,"title":"","content":"One could argue the same ould be said for the dark ages.<br /> <br /> The anarch revolt, the Diablerie of four antideluvians in a short period of time...pretty apocalyptic stuff.<br /> <br /> I mean yes their were literally running gehenna books for revised.<br /> <br /> But unless they want to. Make vampire: the mad max...I doubt that's the way they are gonna go","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T14:06:46-07:00","id":614000,"title":"","content":"I think before in this thread somebody pointed out that they stated it will be post-Gehenna, only they called it &quot;some sort of Gehenna&quot; which means necessarily that it will become a soft one. Unless they simply want to scrap the stuff in Revised - and since they want to advance, not re-write the metaplot, that's not the case - they'll have to keep what they have already made canon and try to deal with what they made happen in the previous editions.<br /> <br /> ...if they will simply call it a &quot;false start&quot; they will immediately devolve most of the attention of the setting as to why that happened at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","user":"Nigredo","date":". 08-03-2015, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","name":"Nigredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T14:06:49-07:00","id":614001,"title":"","content":"This might be crazy talk, but I'd like it if they merged n and c WoD into one universe. Most of requiems stuff can fit into masquerade for sure, and I did love the idea of having a WoD core that each supernatural series branched off of. Both systems could use a massive overhaul mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T14:23:17-07:00","id":614014,"title":"","content":"I'm positively excited. I like the V20 expansions's timeline updates and M20 an W20 very much. I just wish there won't be too big changes in the overall themes and moods of the game(s). I still like the gothic-punkness and always will. I stick with CWoD instead of the (N)WoD because of these and the rich historical background. I want Masquerade to be Masquerade, Ascension as Ascension and so on to the other lines. Updating and advancing are good, changes in the settin are good, these make it breathing and alive. But I don't want absolutely different toned games.<br /> <br /> The rules update is quite promising. I can't count the number of sighs among my frineds like &quot;if we have CWoD with the NWoD rules...&quot; Yes there are the translation guides and they are very good, but they mean WORK. A lot of Work. So I cross fingers and hope for the best new shiny rules systems (including crossover!!!) for the next iteration of CWoD. And if the C20 will use the new rules, the better! I wish now that M20 would come just a little later (which I never thoght I will).<br /> <br /> Also regarding Gehenna, the cyclical version is absolutely more appaeling to me. I have always thinking that the end of the world scenario is somewhat too much. Ancient vampires rising, sure that will be a catastrophe and the status quo will tremble to it's core. It will be the end of the world as we know it for a lot of kindred. But genuine armageddon? Antediluvians was slain in the past, clans died out and new clans emerged and the world moves on. So I picture gehenna as the end of an era, not as the end of the world. And Antes are not dumb. Yes they are awfully strong, but if they go rampage, the mages, the garou, the kuei-jin, the hunters and most importantly, HUMANS will notice and bring everything to stop them. So maybe the grandpas devour a lot of their progeny and wreak havoc between the vamps, but the others maybe noticing it just barely, because the good 'ol dustbags play it hard and smart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 08-03-2015, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T06:14:46-07:00","id":614940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=614014#post614014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm positively excited. I like the V20 expansions's timeline updates and M20 an W20 very much. I just wish there won't be too big changes in the overall themes and moods of the game(s). I still like the gothic-punkness and always will. I stick with CWoD instead of the (N)WoD because of these and the rich historical background. I want Masquerade to be Masquerade, Ascension as Ascension and so on to the other lines. Updating and advancing are good, changes in the settin are good, these make it breathing and alive. But I don't want absolutely different toned games.<br /> <br /> The rules update is quite promising. I can't count the number of sighs among my frineds like &quot;if we have CWoD with the NWoD rules...&quot; Yes there are the translation guides and they are very good, but they mean WORK. A lot of Work. So I cross fingers and hope for the best new shiny rules systems (including crossover!!!) for the next iteration of CWoD. And if the C20 will use the new rules, the better! I wish now that M20 would come just a little later (which I never thoght I will).</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this is an irrational reaction but when I heard this I was a little bitter. I first played VtM when it came out in the 90's, played a while and then put it down. Came back to it during the whole Time of Judgement because I felt nostalgic and excited that a company would effectively end their line in such a manner. Had a great run again, had a lot of fun. Then came NWoD and man, did I like that, VtR especially. V20 was announced and I bought it, for nostalgic reasons, but I'm hardcore VtR at this point. I like that both coexist. But OWoD ended. Sure it had options to continue, and M20 was amazing as an update, but it still felt like it had a beginning, middle and end and I loved it.<br /> <br /> Now I know NWoD will continue, but I cant help but feel this will impact it negatively [again this is a feeling based on no evidence]. I'm already seeing people want to do away with Generation [a mechanic that really establishes the reason for Gehenna and all that] and make some kind of fluctuating power trait. That sounds like Blood Potency to me. VtR plumbed the best of VtM, and now I get the sense it will happen in reverse. Oh sure I can ignore the new game as it may not be for me [I might buy it just to keep up with the metaplot] but how will I ignore it if it takes away the focus, innovation and the creative energy of its newer little brother, now older brother? Whatever VtM 4th ed does I just hope it treads lightly on its counterpart. Keep themes and mechanics of both very distinct.<br /> <br /> What I'm desperate for is an expanded, updated Translation Guide [now I guess I'll have to wait for VtM4 for any chance for that].<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:16:41-07:00","id":615029,"title":"","content":"what I find hard with leaving Generation behind is that even an Ante after millennia of sleep wiould be just slightly better off than a newly embraced. This does not work with several of the gehenna-events: e.g. Zapathustra had to be dealt with by the 3 oldest Bodhisattvas, a techno-nuke and then the sun. Also, it does not work with Ur-Shulgi waking up, snapping his fingers and breaking the Tremere curse on his clan. I liked the idea of a combination of Generation and Blood Potency...that is, until I thought how it would be ill-fitting in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","user":"Nigredo","date":". 08-04-2015, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5483-nigredo","name":"Nigredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T10:01:44-07:00","id":615235,"title":"","content":"If you've read the new Revised Convention Books, you'll get an updated metaplot anyway. In that, a load of weird things happened around the millennium, and things calmed down again. This echoes the Dark Ages setting, where lots happened, and then it all died down until the Final Nights. There's also a suggestion in the MRev Convention Books that this is a slightly different universe to the one in which the ToJ supplements took place--either that ToJ was one possible future (or rather, many) and this one is another, or that the ToJ is at an even further point in the future.<br /> <br /> V4 might do for the oWoD what Rise of the Machines and Salvation did to the Terminator franchise--delay the apocalypse and show us a different possible fate. (Hopefully it'll be far better written that T3 or T4, of course.)<br /> <br /> I suspect that V4 will continue in the same vein as the MRev Con Books, probably with a different metaplot to the BNS/MET stuff, but maybe with some overlapping ideas. Everything up to the ToJ supplements happened, and then a series of supernatural catastrophes cleansed the way for a new age (as per KOTE, ROTDM and that old 2e quote about a cyclical Gehenna), in which vampire society has been shaken but not destroyed. Another Gehenna may come, but perhaps far off into the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:13:02-07:00","id":615323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=614001#post614001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be crazy talk, but I'd like it if they merged n and c WoD into one universe. Most of requiems stuff can fit into masquerade for sure, and I did love the idea of having a WoD core that each supernatural series branched off of. Both systems could use a massive overhaul mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the idea of having a WOD Core as well. It's one of only a handful of things that I think they should bring over to a new edition of Vampire. I'm not so sure that I want to see Requiem rules with Masquerade setting. I like that they're a separate thing. I was disappointed when Masquerade ended and now that it's starting back up I'm glad to hear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/751-dicemauler","name":"dicemauler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:22:23-07:00","id":615379,"title":"","content":"I liked some of the things that were included in Revised as possible alternatives, i.e. Generation being an age-based increase in power rather than intrinsic and static, and possible multiple origins of vampirism. But I like the oWOD system far better than nWOD, with V20 being my favorite permutation of the rules to date. I'm willing to be convinced by further revisions of the system (hopefully not in the direction of V20DA, whose changes I found unanimously inferior to V20), but don't want to see a complete overhaul into the Blood &amp; Smoke system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T11:45:40-07:00","id":615402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=615235#post615235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've read the new Revised Convention Books, you'll get an updated metaplot anyway. In that, a load of weird things happened around the millennium, and things calmed down again. This echoes the Dark Ages setting, where lots happened, and then it all died down until the Final Nights. There's also a suggestion in the MRev Convention Books that this is a slightly different universe to the one in which the ToJ supplements took place--either that ToJ was one possible future (or rather, many) and this one is another, or that the ToJ is at an even further point in the future.<br /> <br /> V4 might do for the oWoD what Rise of the Machines and Salvation did to the Terminator franchise--delay the apocalypse and show us a different possible fate. (Hopefully it'll be far better written that T3 or T4, of course.)<br /> <br /> I suspect that V4 will continue in the same vein as the MRev Con Books, probably with a different metaplot to the BNS/MET stuff, but maybe with some overlapping ideas. Everything up to the ToJ supplements happened, and then a series of supernatural catastrophes cleansed the way for a new age (as per KOTE, ROTDM and that old 2e quote about a cyclical Gehenna), in which vampire society has been shaken but not destroyed. Another Gehenna may come, but perhaps far off into the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I kind of agree with you. The approach of the Rev Ed CBs and some of the metaplot material from M20, early Rev Ed events happened but the end never came, becoming yet another Apocalypse scare is the ideal approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T13:26:38-07:00","id":615504,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to see the oWoD settings revisited in a way that divests itself of all the 90s-ass bullshit and terrible mechanics. oWoD+the ability to take itself seriously with modern sensibilites, both setting and game design=happy me. true reboot. doubt we'll get that, but I wouldn't mind it. the X20 editions have been...too faithful to the originals for my tastes. if I thought something was SUPER COOL when I was a teenager, as I did oWoD, I probably think it's SUPER EMBARRASSING now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1152-crawlkill","name":"crawlkill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T19:09:47-07:00","id":615907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=612956#post612956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the source for this information??</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I should have said that those are *my* ideas for a metaplot 4.0, though I did take into consideration all the clan novels as well as the Gehenna novel. Some things need better explaining though, like , the Assamites were moving politically towards the Camarilla, that is clear in the later clan novels, however, there is a small problem, an 8.000 year old methusalah called Ur Shulgi, who has a 9 in all thaumaturgical paths, meaning that he can turn elders into ash with a blink. In fact thats exactly what he did to the previous old man of the mountain. How could this demi-god get destroyed? I fancied a story myself, Fatima met Haqim, who gave her his magical sword and order her to kill the shepherd as part of some test.<br /> <br /> Don't know, just ideas, trying to make sure we don't leave any loose ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T19:10:48-07:00","id":615908,"title":"","content":"I wasn't a teen and I thought it was pretty awesome when I was introduced to it. I see it as being no less awesome now.<br /> <br /> This announcement excites me a lot. V20 was not a new edition, but I kind of treated it that way. I did a lot of thinking about how the metaplot would evolve, and now it will be interesting to see the direction the developers take. Bring on 4E!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T20:01:02-07:00","id":615936,"title":"","content":"Also, it should be canon that Theo Bell killed Hardestadt. Hardestadt had been behaving like a douche for over 1.000 years, I like that he met his final death at the hands of Theo Bell, while suffering under the effects of the withering. Gods know the Camarilla needs new leadership, people who were brought into the fold al least during the 18th century, no more self-entitled vampire barons with feudal ideas of privilege. Pieterzoon seems like the proper man to become the first Camarilla CEO, a down to earth, hardworking, intelligent vampirel who understand the importance of keeping up the traditions. Also, he has a platonic love affair with Lucita, who, after slaying her own sire Cardinal Mon\u00e7ada, became the prestigious Cardinal of Madrid and is now in a position to challenge for the Sabbat's regency. Could she be helped by Pieterzoon in this endeavour? The assamites would never have been accepted into the Camarilla if Hardestadt was still alive, there is a much bigger chance of this happening under the tutelage of the open minded Pieterzoon, Hardesdat had very little love for the assamites, as they tried to diablerize him several times during the late middle ages, and he was the one who ordered Tremere to curse the Assassins<br /> <br /> Just brainstorming some ideas I've had for years, maybe some actual WW staff will read this and give it a thought : )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","user":"BR_Malk","date":". 08-05-2015, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T06:56:39-07:00","id":616410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crawlkill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=615504#post615504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the X20 editions have been...too faithful to the originals for my tastes. if I thought something was SUPER COOL when I was a teenager, as I did oWoD, I probably think it's SUPER EMBARRASSING now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! Nice way to shit all over the original writers of the Classic World of Darkness! There work should be regarded as super embarrassing!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T07:06:45-07:00","id":616418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BR_Malk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=615936#post615936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it should be canon that Theo Bell killed Hardestadt. Hardestadt had been behaving like a douche for over 1.000 years, I like that he met his final death at the hands of Theo Bell, while suffering under the effects of the withering. Gods know the Camarilla needs new leadership, people who were brought into the fold al least during the 18th century, no more self-entitled vampire barons with feudal ideas of privilege.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, as Tyler discovered, it wouldn't matter. There are plenty more Hardestadts where that one came from <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T07:11:26-07:00","id":618836,"title":"","content":"Things I hope they take from VtR to VtM4:<br /> Streamlined attributes, one resembling Strength, one Dex and one Stamina in each category.<br /> <br /> Things I hope they do NOT take from VtR:<br /> Static difficulties.<br /> Combined Attack &amp; Damage (man is it hard to hit someone with an epee, but hey... this chainsaw is really handy. Wtf?)<br /> Getting rid of multiple actions (I'd rather loosen it up a bit, maybe more like shadowrung 3rd. For example: everyone gets to take an action, afterwards 5 is substracted from everyones Initiative, everyone who still has initiative may take another action, then again 5 is substracted and so on... and celerity gives you maybe... 3 points of initiative per dot? Base initiative would be something like Dex+Wits).<br /> <br /> For me Shadowrun 4th and VtR both made similar changes to the game mechanics that sucked really bad in comparison to what was before. So I really hope they not only keep the world cWoD but also keep a feeling of cWoD in the ruleset, even if there may be major changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:41:23-07:00","id":620947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eadee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=618836#post618836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combined Attack &amp; Damage (man is it hard to hit someone with an epee, but hey... this chainsaw is really handy. Wtf?)</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, they did a slick redo of this in nWoD 2nd edition. Weapons now have a static damage score. So, you roll [stat]+[skill]-[defense] to hit, and if you hit, damage is [successes]+[weapon damage]-[soak rating]. This gets rid of their weird quirk where chainsaws were easier to hit with than epees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","name":"trudge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1026_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T05:49:21-07:00","id":622082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trudge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=620947#post620947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, they did a slick redo of this in nWoD 2nd edition. Weapons now have a static damage score. So, you roll [stat]+[skill]-[defense] to hit, and if you hit, damage is [successes]+[weapon damage]-[soak rating]. This gets rid of their weird quirk where chainsaws were easier to hit with than epees.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that sounds better indeed. Allthough I prefer a separate roll for defense as well I could live with something like that. Static soak is fine for me as well as static damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T09:16:47-07:00","id":622348,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to bash on V20, V:tR, any developers, writers, etc. and so forth. Way too early to have an opinion. Wait and see.<br /> <br /> Still, I can't resist one little dig - please forgive me...<br /> <br /> Does this mean we're going to have four different metaplot settings for the new corebook, or are we finally getting one official version of Gehenna?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7242-velvet-elvis","name":"Velvet Elvis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T13:03:58-07:00","id":622582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Velvet Elvis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=622348#post622348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or are we finally getting one official version of Gehenna?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure we're going to get the one true Gehenna. And it won't be any of those in the Gehenna book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3117-lucius","name":"Lucius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T14:43:45-07:00","id":622683,"title":"","content":"If they base it on &quot;Fair Is Foul,&quot; I am done with Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T15:09:46-07:00","id":622707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=622683#post622683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they base it on &quot;Fair Is Foul,&quot; I am done with Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>what happend in fair is foul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T16:15:44-07:00","id":622785,"title":"","content":"I doubt the Gehenna that happened in 4th Edition will be any of the scenarios in ToJ: Gehenna.<br /> <br /> This is just my pure speculation, but I'm expecting some kind of Withering happened. It probably didn't completely wipe out all vampires everywhere, but it probably significantly impacted their population, enough to shake up the remains of society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The flight plan I just filed with the Agency lists Smee, Mai Min, Dr. Pavelheer, but only Juan Ovyu!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7178-cia","name":"CIA","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7178_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T21:44:15-07:00","id":623099,"title":"","content":"My expectation is that they'll use Gehanna to do some house cleaning, and remove some of the more troublesome NPCs, bloodlines, and clans, and maybe some big revisions, like major changes to how some disciplines work.<br /> <br /> The details of Gehenna would be whatever supports those decisions. That's what I'd do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=622707#post622707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what happend in fair is foul?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, it turned Gehenna into a fight between Caine and Lilith, with the 13 antediluvians more or less supporting Caine, while 7 new antes supported Lilith. The PCs went on a McGuffin hunt for &quot;the last daughter of eve,&quot; which turned out to be a homeless girl with a crescent moon birthmark. Then there was a big melee between all of the ancient vampire gods, followed by some vampires getting returned to human and the rest just dying.<br /> <br /> I think it was mostly there for players who preferred Revelations of the Dark Mother over the Book of Nod as their vampire bible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1026-trudge","name":"trudge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1026_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T16:18:26-07:00","id":623739,"title":"","content":"Unofficially, the Wormwood scenario has been seen as the &quot;canon&quot; ending by White Wolf, though I'm not sure where Onyx Path falls on it, or if perhaps it only &quot;ended&quot; the Revised line in their view. VTM4 may be closer in line to the Revised core book, thematically, with Gehenna being more akin to the Y2K scare (remember that one?), turning back the clock to the eve of the &quot;real&quot; Gehenna. Honestly, while I doubt that VTM4 will take the same &quot;meta plot agnostic&quot; tack that V20 did, Onyx Path may decide that several events that occurred simply... did not. They may decide that anything after New York by Night is no longer canon, or maybe nothing outside the core and Clan books are canon any longer. Additionally, VTM4 is a new edition. Semantically, the meta plot is a hallmark of Revised; VTM4 only needs to include the moods, themes, and set pieces (remember: meta plot does not equal setting). For reference, look at other role playing games and the differences in their editions. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 08-11-2015, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T19:14:27-07:00","id":626145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/609481-vampire-the-masquerade-4th-edition-announced-at-gencon?p=623739#post623739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unofficially, the Wormwood scenario has been seen as the &quot;canon&quot; ending by White Wolf...</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? The worst of all of them is the official one? Sweet zombie jesus...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T00:14:42-07:00","id":626374,"title":"","content":"Or they may just move gehenna forward (&quot;like current in game time + X) and continue pre-gehenna storyline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4807-elotar","name":"elotar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T16:11:56-07:00","id":637499,"title":"","content":"Great news!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7441-matheus-